ject-level panels establish feasible investment bounds rather than exact rule rankings.\\\\\\\",\\n+  \\\\\\\"narrative_rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"This is a bounded counterfactual empirical study, not a new optimizer or training study. Existing final decision records support a direct rule-by-response comparison, including an exact matched-cohort reversal on the six-task Open LLM panel and explicit uncertainty about optimal support on the 57-subject HELM panel. The same scientific question organizes these as complementary evidence blocks with different certificate strength, not as transfer or discovery-order experiments. The frozen reference procedure is the studied method; unsuccessful search proposals are not the contribution. No universal ordering, practical training cost, or causal contamination effect is inferred.\\\\\\\",\\n+  \\\\\\\"prior_paper_story_status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rejected\\\\\\\",\\n+  \\\\\\\"edit_framing_decision\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No edit context, previous_paper directory, prior manuscript, aggregated directory, or extra_tasks directory is staged. The rejected status denotes rejection of an assumed inherited improvement story, not rejection of an actual manuscript. Compare three alternatives explicitly: preserve an optimizer-improvement story, broaden to a shared novel certificate family, or recenter on response-dependent investment comparisons. Choose the third: no search improvement was selected, component ablations are absent, and exact rule contrasts are stronger than claims of algorithmic novelty.\\\\\\\",\\n+  \\\\\\\"staged_input_impact\\\\\\\": [\\n+    \\\\\\\"Directly inspected source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py and the baseline counterpart; their source files are identical. The selected procedure exhausts panels with at most six coordinates, uses sorted headroom for larger mean panels, and marginal-score greedy supports for larger median and trimmed-mean panels.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Read final_evaluation independently of downstream_study. Its completed, qualified evaluation supports a finished empirical study; it does not establish population generalization or solver novelty.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"The ordinary primary six-task records contain exact support outcomes, whereas the 57-subject median and trimmed-mean records retain bounded support outcomes. This changes the center of gravity from solver improvement to aggregation sensitivity with explicit certificate scope.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"The separate auxiliary BBH and six-coordinate projections add sensitivity and verification depth, not a new architecture, new model training condition, or a pooled primary benchmark.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"The local ICLR style is single-column, with a 5.5-inch text width and 9-inch text height. This supports full-text-width, low-density comparisons rather than two-column dashboard figures.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"The supplied bibliography contains metadata retrieval records, many tangential to this study, without evidence of substantive reading. Its presence does not license scientific positioning or citation padding. No external source was accessed during strategy generation.\\\\\\\"\\n+  ],\\n+  \\\\\\\"method_groups\\\\\\\": [\\n+    {\\n+      \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Frozen bounded-headroom support-minimization procedure\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"role\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"supporting\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"include_reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"This is the selected studied procedure, not a newly successful proposal: improve selected coordinates by alpha times their remaining headroom, hold rivals fixed, and report exact support, certified infeasibility, or an honest lower–upper support interval. Explain exhaustive small-panel search, exact mean sorting, and larger-panel greedy witnesses separately.\\\\\\\"\\n+    },\\n+    {\\n+      \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Equal-task arithmetic mean\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"role\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"baseline\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"include_reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Provides the directly grounded aggregation comparator and an analytically exact sorted-headroom solution; retain it in every main rule comparison.\\\\\\\"\\n+    },\\n+    {\\n+      \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Conventional median\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"role\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"supporting\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"include_reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The central exact six-task contrast uses the conventional median, including the average of the two middle values for an even task count; distinguish this from a lower or upper median.\\\\\\\"\\n+    },\\n+    {\\n+      \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Symmetric 20-percent trimmed mean\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"role\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"supporting\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"include_reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Provides the grounded intermediate order-statistic condition: remove floor(m/5) values from each tail. It checks whether the evidence is specific to the median without extending to untested ordinal rules.\\\\\\\"\\n+    },\\n+    {\\n+      \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No-intervention, seeded-random, and marginal-score-greedy investment policies\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"role\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"baseline\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"include_reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"These comparators already have matched final decision records. They contextualize support selection, retain zero and negative differences, and show that the selected procedure coincides with greedy in important regimes. They are not component ablations or independent model-training methods.\\\\\\\"\\n+    }\\n+  ],\\n+  \\\\\\\"results_focus\\\\\\\": [\\n+    \\\\\\\"Primary thesis test: ordinary Open LLM primary decisions only; match by seed and target slot and retain targets attainable under both mean and median at alpha=0.5 and alpha=1.0. Compare exact support fractions on that identical per-seed cohort across both response conditions. The recorded data give a negative median-minus-mean average at half headroom and a positive average at full headroom for every final seed. This is a descriptive within-snapshot reversal, not a pre-registered significance claim.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Report attainability for all sampled ordinary primary targets at alpha=0.25, 0.5, and 1.0, separately for HELM and Open LLM, so conditioning the exact contrast on attainable cases cannot conceal infeasible targets.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Report support cost with exactness attached: exact support for the six-task panel and the mean, but evaluator lower bounds and selected feasible upper bounds for larger median/trimmed panels. A reversal of greedy witness costs on HELM must not be called a reversal of minimum costs when bound intervals overlap.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Retain matched policy comparisons, preferably a compact main table at alpha=0.5 and the complete grid after references. State where exact selection reduces support relative to greedy and where it ties. Existing paired intervals compare the selected procedure against random or greedy; they are not cross-rule confidence intervals.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Keep constant-ceiling, zero-response, permutation, and replay checks separate from ordinary performance. A passed check establishes only the property tested, not universal scientific validity or optimality.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Use auxiliary six-coordinate projections and revision-matched BBH decisions only as separately labeled sensitivity evidence. Do not merge them with primary scores, compare their target slots as identical model identities, or claim domain transfer.\\\\\\\"\\n+  ],\\n+  \\\\\\\"figure_plan\\\\\\\": [\\n+    \\\\\\\"Figure 1, early overview: fixed public task scores and rivals; target-only bounded-headroom intervention; three aggregation rules leading to exact support, infeasibility, or an interval. No fabricated score matrix or illustrative numerical result.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Figure 2, central exact comparison: two matched-cohort dot plots, one for half headroom and one for full headroom, showing median-minus-mean minimum-support fraction by final sampling seed with a zero reference line.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Figure 3, scope and cost: a 2-by-2 composite with one row per primary panel family, all-target attainability at three response ceilings on the left, and paired attainable-cohort support bounds at half/full headroom on the right. Exact values and unresolved intervals use visibly different marks.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Use tables, not additional main figures, for snapshot scope, comparator differences, and certificate/status counts. Put the full conditional comparator-interval grid and auxiliary sensitivities after references.\\\\\\\"\\n+  ],\\n+  \\\\\\\"figure_specs\\\\\\\": [\\n+    {\\n+      \\\\\\\"figure_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"investment_overview\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"required\\\\\\\": true,\\n+      \\\\\\\"purpose\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Make the counterfactual investment object, fixed-rival assumption, aggregation conditions, and certificate outcomes legible before quantitative results.\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"figure_type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"diagram\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"preferred_generator\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"generate-concept-figure\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"group_by\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"score intervention and certificate scope\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"metric\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"none; qualitative specification only\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"split_by\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"fixed scores, bounded intervention, aggregation and support outcome\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"preferred_span\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"full_width\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"target_width_fraction\\\\\\\": 1.0,\\n+      \\\\\\\"layout_rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"In the inspected single-column ICLR style, full width is 5.5 inches, not a two-column spread. Use a shallow approximately 5.5-by-1.8-inch diagram on page 1 or 2; a half-width 2.75-inch rendering would compress the update equation and outcome labels. Keep at most six visual groups and three aggregator branches, with at least 9-point rendered labels.\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"allow_progression\\\\\\\": false,\\n+      \\\\\\\"max_panels\\\\\\\": 1,\\n+      \\\\\\\"max_panels_per_row\\\\\\\": 1,\\n+      \\\\\\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\\\\\": 6,\\n+      \\\\\\\"max_series_per_panel\\\\\\\": 3,\\n+      \\\\\\\"source_ids\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\\\\\"],\\n+      \\\\\\\"content_constraints\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Show x_j changing to x_j+alpha(1-x_j) only on the selected support and label rivals fixed. Three aggregators are conditions, not sequential improvements. Distinguish exact, infeasible, and bounded outcomes. Do not draw training, an architecture transition, a novel certificate mechanism, or numerical toy measurements.\\\\\\\"\\n+    },\\n+    {\\n+      \\\\\\\"figure_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"exact_rule_contrast\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"required\\\\\\\": true,\\n+      \\\\\\\"purpose\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Display the exact within-snapshot mean–median ordering reversal without infeasibility penalties, composition changes across response conditions, or search chronology.\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"figure_type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"paired_difference_dotplot\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"preferred_generator\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"matplotlib\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"group_by\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"final sampling seed\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"metric\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"mean exact median-minus-mean support fraction on a fixed jointly attainable cohort\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"split_by\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"alpha=0.5 versus alpha=1.0 on the ordinary Open LLM primary panel\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"preferred_span\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"full_width\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"target_width_fraction\\\\\\\": 1.0,\\n+      \\\\\\\"layout_rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Two side-by-side panels occupy approximately 5.5 by 2.1 inches in the 5.5-inch single text column. Each panel has three seed categories and one contrast series, so 9-point labels and a common signed y scale remain readable; include a horizontal zero line and cohort counts in the caption. Do not connect response conditions as a time trajectory.\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"allow_progression\\\\\\\": false,\\n+      \\\\\\\"max_panels\\\\\\\": 2,\\n+      \\\\\\\"max_panels_per_row\\\\\\\": 2,\\n+      \\\\\\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\\\\\": 3,\\n+      \\\\\\\"max_series_per_panel\\\\\\\": 1,\\n+      \\\\\\\"source_ids\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\\\\\"],\\n+      \\\\\\\"content_constraints\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Filter ordinary primary Open LLM decisions, join rule/alpha cells by seed and slot, and intersect attainability under both rules at both response conditions. Each seed retains the same cohort in both panels. Plot exact support-count differences divided by six; show individual seed summaries, not invented confidence intervals or a pooled population p-value.\\\\\\\"\\n+    },\\n+    {\\n+      \\\\\\\"figure_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"attainability_and_support_scope\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"required\\\\\\\": true,\\n+      \\\\\\\"purpose\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Show which targets can attain first place and how much support is established, while exposing differences between exact and bounded evidence.\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"figure_type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"attainment_points_and_support_intervals\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"preferred_generator\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"matplotlib\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"group_by\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"aggregation rule\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"metric\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"left: target attainment rate; right: normalized support lower and feasible upper bounds\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"split_by\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"HELM 57-subject panel versus Open LLM six-task panel\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"preferred_span\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"full_width\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"target_width_fraction\\\\\\\": 1.0,\\n+      \\\\\\\"layout_rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"A 2-by-2 figure at approximately 5.5 by 3.4 inches uses the full single-column width. Two panels per row, three ceiling categories at most, three rule series, shared scales, and a common legend avoid shrinking a dashboard. Use at least 9-point final labels and a short caption explicitly defining the support cohorts and interval semantics.\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"allow_progression\\\\\\\": false,\\n+      \\\\\\\"max_panels\\\\\\\": 4,\\n+      \\\\\\\"max_panels_per_row\\\\\\\": 2,\\n+      \\\\\\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\\\\\": 3,\\n+      \\\\\\\"max_series_per_panel\\\\\\\": 3,\\n+      \\\\\\\"source_ids\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\\\\\"],\\n+      \\\\\\\"content_constraints\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Left panels include every ordinary primary target at all three recorded ceilings and use one attainment definition: a verified strict-first support with a supported claim. Right panels use only alpha=0.5 and 1.0, intersect attainable targets across all three rules within each seed and ceiling, and report the cohort sizes. Average the within-seed lower and upper support fractions with declared equal seed weights; the interval is an identification/certification range, not a confidence interval. Cohorts here may differ across ceilings, unlike Figure 2. Exact costs collapse to points. Never draw the infeasible sentinel m+1 as an actual cost. If a required joint cohort is empty, show not estimable rather than imputation.\\\\\\\"\\n+    }\\n+  ],\\n+  \\\\\\\"supplementary_plan\\\\\\\": {\\n+    \\\\\\\"purpose\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Provide substantive mathematical, conditional-uncertainty, sensitivity, and reproducibility depth after references without hiding the central exact contrast, unattainability, or larger-panel certification limits from the main body.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"planned_subsections\\\\\\\": [\\n+      {\\n+        \\\\\\\"heading\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Support objective, aggregation conventions, and certificates\\\\\\\",\\n+        \\\\\\\"grounded_content\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Give the complete target-only objective, strict-first tolerance, even median and trimming conventions, mean sorted-headroom argument, exhaustive six-coordinate procedure, full-uplift infeasibility test, and the conservative lower-bound versus feasible-witness distinction. Tie explanations to the inspected frozen source and task/evaluate_final.py; do not describe abandoned bounds as evaluated contributions.\\\\\\\",\\n+        \\\\\\\"source_ids\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\\\\\"]\\n+      },\\n+      {\\n+        \\\\\\\"heading\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Complete rule-by-response and comparator tables\\\\\\\",\\n+        \\\\\\\"grounded_content\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Tabulate ordinary primary decisions by family, seed, rule, and ceiling, retaining attainment counts, exact/interval status, lower bounds, feasible support sizes, and all zero/random/greedy references. Include the already-recorded per-seed cluster-percentile intervals for selected-minus-random and selected-minus-greedy effort, their conditional scope and all null effects; do not reinterpret them as cross-rule inference.\\\\\\\",\\n+        \\\\\\\"source_ids\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"final.metric.feasible_rate\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"final.metric.mean_effort_fraction\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"final.metric.mean_verified_gap_fraction\\\\\\\"]\\n+      },\\n+      {\\n+        \\\\\\\"heading\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Task granularity and auxiliary sensitivity\\\\\\\",\\n+        \\\\\\\"grounded_content\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Separate auxiliary six-task projections from the BBH subtask subset using family, panel, and slot routing in task/evaluate_final.py. Report the already-recorded auxiliary outcomes, revision reconciliation, and distinct evaluation-setting caveat. No new resampling experiment, unrun ablation, or causal granularity attribution is promised.\\\\\\\",\\n+        \\\\\\\"source_ids\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\\\\\"]\\n+      },\\n+      {\\n+        \\\\\\\"heading\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Matched controls and evaluation scope\\\\\\\",\\n+        \\\\\\\"grounded_content\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Describe constant-ceiling, zero-response, column-permutation and reset-replay checks, including replay statistical weight zero. Report the completed final qualification faithfully and explain that it does not prove every minimum-support statement or independent benchmark generalization. Retain the evidence trust limitation rather than promoting candidate diagnostics into verified facts.\\\\\\\",\\n+        \\\\\\\"source_ids\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"final.metric.control_pass_rate\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"final.qualification.status\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"final.qualification.outcome\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"final.qualification.correct\\\\\\\"]\\n+      },\\n+      {\\n+        \\\\\\\"heading\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Frozen selection and unsuccessful alternatives\\\\\\\",\\n+        \\\\\\\"grounded_content\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Provide a concise nonchronological disclosure of baseline selection, zero search-score change, three scored alternatives, and zero unscored alternatives. None was a qualifying search winner. Report unsuccessful outcomes without inventing a defect, adaptivity explanation, or measured loss for absent evidence; keep search quantities separate from final measurements.\\\\\\\",\\n+        \\\\\\\"source_ids\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"study.selection_kind\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"study.investigation_outcome\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"study.search_score_delta\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"study.attempts.total\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"study.attempts.scored\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"study.attempts.unscored\\\\\\\"]\\n+      },\\n+      {\\n+        \\\\\\\"heading\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Public data provenance and reproduction map\\\\\\\",\\n+        \\\\\\\"grounded_content\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Use existing source records and manifest to document HELM release, the two pinned Open LLM revisions, acquisition time, source and extracted-record hashes, normalization, alias grouping, filtering, target strata, seeds, dependency versions, and CPU commands. Map every eventual plot/table to its derived-data script and source slice; mark those scripts as a writer-stage deliverable, not already present. State unresolved score-data redistribution licensing and variable evaluation settings.\\\\\\\",\\n+        \\\\\\\"source_ids\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\\\\\"]\\n+      },\\n+      {\\n+        \\\\\\\"heading\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"LLM Usage\\\\\\\",\\n+        \\\\\\\"grounded_content\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Disclose the documented LLM role in research ideation, code preparation, reference-query planning, and manuscript framing; add writing/figure assistance only when actually used. State that counterfactual score edits are not model training. Do not invent model identities, provider details, human validation, or a literature-exposure history.\\\\\\\",\\n+        \\\\\\\"source_ids\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"study.selection_kind\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"study.attempts.total\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\\\\\"]\\n+      }\\n+    ]\\n+  },\\n+  \\\\\\\"forbidden_headings\\\\\\\": [\\n+    \\\\\\\"Search Progression\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Campaign Phases\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Milestones\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"First Valid Result\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Timeline\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Experiment A\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Experiment B\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"From Baseline to Winner\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Optimization Breakthroughs\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Successful Certificate Variants\\\\\\\"\\n+  ],\\n+  \\\\\\\"forbidden_phrases\\\\\\\": [\\n+    \\\\\\\"we then tried\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"first valid result\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"subsequent improvements\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"next-best\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"later variants\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"winning implementation\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"state of the art\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"universally most robust aggregation\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"median always requires more investment\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"measured training cost\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"causal contamination effect\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"all full-panel solutions are optimal\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"correctness rate\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"correct and eligible\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"eligible\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"combined_score\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"rubric\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"worker_01\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"worker_02\\\\\\\"\\n+  ],\\n+  \\\\\\\"notes_for_writer\\\\\\\": [\\n+    \\\\\\\"Format contract: target the provided ICLR 2026 single-column style and anonymized review format. The inspected paper.sty declares textwidth 5.5in and textheight 9in. Here preferred_span=full_width means the one full text column; a column-width two-column convention does not apply. Do not replace the venue with the NeurIPS template mentioned in source-task provenance.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Body plan: aim for about 8.5 substantive pages, excluding references: 1.25 pages for abstract/introduction and contribution scope, 0.75 for safely grounded related work and modeling context, 1.0 for objective/assumptions, 1.0 for solver and certificate scope, 0.75 for experimental protocol and uncertainty, 2.75 for exact contrast/attainability/support/comparators including figures, and 1.0 for limitations and conclusion. Figure area is included, not added on top. An eight-page body must fill at least 75 percent of its last page; never pad to reach this threshold.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Suggested thesis-first headings: Introduction; Related Work and Scope; Bounded-Response Investment; Computing Support and Certifying Limits; Public Score Panels and Comparison Protocol; Response-Dependent Aggregation Costs; Attainability and Certificate Scope; Limitations and Conclusion. No campaign-order sections.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Define x in [0,1], selected support S, target update x_j+alpha(1-x_j) for j in S, fixed competitors, and unique first as aggregate(target)>max rival aggregate+1e-10. Investment is |S|, normalized by panel task count for cross-panel display. Total normalized score lift is secondary and is not training examples, compute, dollars, or contamination severity. Alpha is a stipulated response fraction, not an estimated learning curve.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"State equal task weighting, no spillover or regression on untouched coordinates, fixed rival pool, and score normalization explicitly. A support-cardinality comparison across six tasks and 57 subjects does not equate their real-world intervention costs. Avoid interpreting named architectures or task metadata as controlled architecture experiments.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Private-only grounding audit: final.qualification.status=completed, final.qualification.outcome=qualified, and final.qualification.correct=true are authoritative for final qualification, read independently from study.final.*. Preserve this assessment during writing, review, audit, and revision; if later authoritative qualification differs, disclose failure and limitations rather than keeping this positive label. Qualification is neither a novelty certificate nor generalization evidence.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Private-only selection audit: study.selection_kind=baseline, study.investigation_outcome=completed_no_winner, study.search_score_delta=0, study.attempts.scored=3 and study.attempts.unscored=0. The frozen source equals the original baseline source. Keep search scores and final scores in their separate scopes. Failed alternatives have no grounded failure-cause diagnosis; do not choose between performance, validity, or adaptivity explanations without additional evaluator evidence.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Private-only final evidence audit: final.evidence.episodes is the quantitative source for every planned rule-specific comparison and recorded paired interval. It contains final seeds 1009, 1013, and 1019. Its candidate_diagnostics_trust is unverified. The source file checksum matches the manifest, and the final evaluator computes witness checks and small-panel audits, but do not promote any unverified candidate diagnostic or the exact_audit_pass field alone into a universal exactness claim. Attach explicit source slices and evaluator conventions to every derived result.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Private-only descriptive cohort check, derived from existing final records, not a new experiment: Figure 2 retains 18, 17, and 17 targets for seeds 1009, 1013, and 1019. Median-minus-mean support-fraction averages are respectively -0.129630, -0.127451, -0.068627 at alpha=0.5 and +0.138889, +0.127451, +0.156863 at alpha=1.0. Recompute from selected support counts in the plotting script rather than hard-coding these rounded audit values. This subset analysis is descriptive and was chosen during framing.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Private-only metric semantics: final.metric.mean_effort_fraction uses a value of one for nonattainment, so it is a penalized summary, not the mean minimum investment of successful targets. final.metric.mean_verified_gap_fraction is relative to a verified lower bound and is not necessarily true optimizer error. Do not use these aggregates as substitutes for the paired cohort analysis or mix control cases into ordinary-result plots.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Uncertainty contract: final sampling seeds reuse fixed public panels and may share targets or model ancestry; they are not independent training replicates. Existing paired intervals use 200 cluster resamples with RNG seed 48271 and are conditional on fixed snapshots/rival pools. Keep all three seed summaries visible or tabulated. No existing cross-rule interval or p-value supports the reversal, and baseline intervals cannot be reassigned to it.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Main tables: a compact scope table distinguishing public source snapshots from the evaluated extracted panels; an investment/certificate table with cohort sizes and infeasible counts; and a matched policy-difference table at alpha=0.5 for both families and all three rules. Include ties with greedy; put the complete already-recorded interval grid after references. These are planned transformations of existing records, not unperformed experiments.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"The main body must retain the exact six-task comparison, unconditional attainment rates, conditioning definitions, larger-panel interval caveat, uncertainty scope, and failed-search disclosure in brief. Supplementary material expands them; it must not hide contradictory or essential evidence. Route any separately supplied authoritative appendix-ranked analyses after references without inventing a ranking or retroactively changing this strategy.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Provenance contract: HELM v1.13.0; Open LLM contents revision 9c09a7cae43334062a82cb164f2ef255013dafa2; separate results revision aa81ecc38fdc5708254b833923368970efdf5ef5. The final manifest records acquisition on 2026-11-17 and extracted records SHA-256 d80abb1b13c6962e15f04d9794fc18fcf39e91cf7c79c679e233d3031f934398. Use task/resources/final/manifest.json and records.json for source/normalization/license details. Do not claim evaluation of every row in the public repositories.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"BBH scope: the existing manifest records model-revision reconciliation but explicitly says contents and results are distinct runs with potentially different settings. Auxiliary Open LLM odd slots route to BBH and even slots to the primary-family projection. Use the routing code to separate them, not the generic auxiliary label alone. BBH is not an independent replicated transfer benchmark.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Literature contract: cite only existing bibliography keys after safely reading the actual permitted source; retrieval metadata is not substantive reading. Many supplied entries are tangential, and several relevant starter records are absent, so bibliography curation and safe substantive reading remain writer-stage prerequisites before related-work claims. Do not fill space with unrelated citations or claim novelty against unread papers. Never search for the prohibited study, expand citation graphs, or infer its identity; log and stop any accidental exposure.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Figure production contract: only the overview uses generate-concept-figure, retaining editable source and prompt provenance. This stage plans figures and does not run that workflow. Quantitative figures must be script-generated vector PDF plus 300-DPI PNG; use the PDF in LaTeX whenever it exists. For a raster-only overview, regenerate at at least 2400 pixels wide at full width, or at least 1200 pixels if a later justified column-width placement is chosen; never upscale. Keep rendered labels at least 9pt and simplify rather than shrinking dense figures.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Keep artifact and internal decision terminology private. Reader-facing terms are target attainment rate, support fraction, strict first place, exact minimum support, certified infeasibility, and feasible support interval. Do not turn the selected reference into a novel learned method, or experimental controls into scientific success rates.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Required separate LLM Usage disclosure belongs after references if needed; remove names, affiliations, acknowledgements, funding statements, and identifying repository links. Describe only actual assistance documented in run artifacts. Do not claim human checks, literature reading, or training that did not occur.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"This strategy creates neither a manuscript nor claim-mapping artifacts, generates no figures, performs no new research experiment, and does not run final-paper validation. A ready framing is not a claim that manuscript reproduction scripts, substantive citation verification, or a compiled paper already exist.\\\\\\\"\\n+  ],\\n+  \\\\\\\"failure_reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\n+}\\n*** Add File: /workspace/paper/paper_strategy.md\\n+# Paper strategy: response ceilings and targeted investment\\n+\\n+**Status:** ready. **Prompt family:** \\\"'`paper_standalone` / `write-paper-standalone`.\\n+**Provisional title:** Response Ceilings and Targeted Investment in Multitask Leaderboards.\\n+\\n+## Scientific center\\n+\\n+**Question.** Under a bounded, target-only score-response model with fixed rivals, how many task coordinates must be improved to attain strict first place, and how does that investment depend on the aggregation rule and response ceiling?\\n+\\n+**Thesis.** In the evaluated public score panels, aggregation robustness is conditional on the response ceiling: exact six-task results reverse the mean–median minimum-support ordering between half and full headroom on matched attainable targets, while larger subject-level panels establish feasible investment bounds rather than exact rule rankings.\\n+\\n+This is a standalone conditional empirical study, not an optimizer breakthrough, a training experiment, or a search report. Organize the six-task and subject-level panels as complementary evidence blocks under one question. Their certificate strength differs; neither is evidence of architecture change or domain transfer. The contribution is the precisely defined investment comparison and its measured limits, not a claim that familiar enumeration or greedy selection is new.\\n+\\n+## Framing decision and rejected alternatives\\n+\\n+No edit-context file, previous manuscript, `previous_paper/`, `aggregated/`, or `extra_tasks/` is staged. The JSON status `prior_paper_story_status: rejected` rejects an assumed inherited improvement narrative; there is no actual prior manuscript to reject.\\n+\\n+| Candidate framing | Decision and grounded reason |\\n+| --- | --- |\\n+| Preserve an optimizer-improvement story | Reject: the frozen selection is the reference baseline, not a successful new optimizer. |\\n+| Broaden to a shared novel certificate family | Reject: no component ablations substantiate the abandoned proposal mechanisms, and large-panel median/trimmed costs are not exact. |\\n+| Recenter on response-dependent investment | Choose: final ordinary decision records support direct rule-by-ceiling comparisons, including exact paired contrasts and explicit unattainability. |\\n+\\n+Direct inspection confirms that the staged selected and baseline source files are identical. Their small-panel enumeration, exact mean sorting, and larger-panel greedy witnesses determine what can be claimed. The auxiliary projections and BBH records provide additional scope checks, not a reason to broaden the thesis to a new method family. The venue changes presentation, not the scientific conclusion.\\n+\\n+## Private grounding and qualification audit\\n+\\n+This section is a provenance memo, not manuscript prose. Use these registered source identifiers in downstream claim mapping:\\n+\\n+- `final.qualification.status = completed`, `final.qualification.outcome = qualified`, and `final.qualification.correct = true`. These come from `paper_data.json.final_evaluation`, read independently of selection metadata. Qualification does not establish novelty, population generalization, or every support minimum.\\n+- `study.selection_kind = baseline`; `study.investigation_outcome = completed_no_winner`; `study.search_score_delta = 0`; `study.attempts.scored = 3`; `study.attempts.unscored = 0`. Search evidence and final measurements have distinct scopes. No search alternative has an established qualifying improvement. Missing performance evidence would not be a measured loss.\\n+- `final.evidence.episodes` contains three sampling seeds, ordinary and matched-control cases, primary and auxiliary decisions, and policy-comparison intervals. Its `candidate_diagnostics_trust` remains `unverified`. The evidence-file SHA-256 agrees with the manifest. Direct evaluator inspection shows witness verification and exhaustive small-panel reference computation; that does not license unrelated candidate diagnostics. The field `exact_audit_pass` alone is not proof of full-panel exactness.\\n+- Preserve the final qualification assessment through writing, review, audit, and revision. If authoritative later evidence changes it to a failure, disclose that failure explicitly and retain its limitations. Failed search alternatives have no established causal diagnosis: do not infer performance-only, validity, or adaptivity failure from a boolean outcome.\\n+\\n+The cross-rule cohort check was a read-only summary of existing records, not a new experiment. Restrict to ordinary primary Open LLM decisions and join on seed and target slot. Intersect targets attainable under both mean and median at both half and full headroom. The resulting fixed cohorts contain 18, 17, and 17 targets for seeds 1009, 1013, and 1019. The following rounded values are audit checks derived from `final.evidence.episodes`, not hard-coded plotting inputs:\\n+\\n+| Sampling seed | Median minus mean support fraction, half headroom | Same contrast, full headroom |\\n+| --- | ---: | ---: |\\n+| 1009 | -0.129630 | +0.138889 |\\n+| 1013 | -0.127451 | +0.127451 |\\n+| 1019 | -0.068627 | +0.156863 |\\n+\\n+All feasible primary six-task costs in this contrast have exact support status and correspond to the frozen exhaustive procedure. The reversal is a descriptive within-snapshot result selected during framing, not a preregistered significance finding. Larger-panel HELM witness-cost reversals are not minimum-cost reversals when certification intervals overlap.\\n+\\n+## Scope and method groups\\n+\\n+Define scores in `[0,1]`, a target model, a fixed rival pool, a task panel of size `m`, and selected support `S`. Only selected coordinates change, by `x_j -> x_j + alpha(1-x_j)`, with recorded `alpha` values `0.25`, `0.5`, and `1.0`. Unique first means target aggregate exceeds the largest rival aggregate by more than `1e-10`. Investment is `|S|`, with `|S|/m` used for normalized display. Total normalized score lift is secondary, not dollars, training examples, or compute.\\n+\\n+Include only these method groups:\\n+\\n+1. **Frozen support-minimization procedure — supporting.** Exhaust at most six coordinates, sort headroom for larger means, and construct marginal-score-greedy supports for larger median/trimmed panels. Explain the all-coordinate infeasibility test and exact versus lower–upper outcomes.\\n+2. **Equal-task arithmetic mean — aggregation baseline.** Retain throughout; the headroom solution is exact.\\n+3. **Conventional median — supporting condition.** Average the two middle scores on even panels; do not substitute a different median convention.\\n+4. **Symmetric 20-percent trimmed mean — supporting condition.** Remove `floor(m/5)` scores from each tail.\\n+5. **No-intervention, seeded-random, and marginal-score-greedy policies — selection baselines.** Keep matched recorded comparisons, including ties. They are not component ablations.\\n+\\n+Do not require discarded rank-window or clipped-envelope branches in the main narrative. No evaluated Borda condition, equilibrium model, measured training response, architecture intervention, or unrun ablation belongs in this paper. State equal task weights, no spillover, no score regression outside the support, fixed rivals, and uncertain mapping from score uplift to actual training investment.\\n+\\n+## Results structure and uncertainty\\n+\\n+Lead with the exact fixed-cohort mean–median contrast. Follow it with all-target attainability and support/certificate scope for both primary families. Maintain one definition of **target attainment rate**: the fraction of ordinary primary target decisions with a verified strict-first support and a supported claim. Do not mix controls into that rate.\\n+\\n+Use a compact main comparator table at half headroom for both families and all three rules, retaining ties with greedy and comparisons against random and no intervention. The complete rule/ceiling/seed grid and all recorded comparator intervals belong after references. A meaningful exact-selection advantage in one small-panel condition does not make the frozen reference a newly invented optimizer.\\n+\\n+The main body must distinguish:\\n+\\n+- Exact six-task and mean minimum costs from larger median/trimmed feasible upper bounds and verified lower bounds.\\n+- Unattainable cases from unresolved support intervals. Never draw the `m+1` infeasibility sentinel as an actual intervention cost.\\n+- Successful-target support from a penalized effort summary: `final.metric.mean_effort_fraction` assigns one to nonattainment. Likewise, `final.metric.mean_verified_gap_fraction` measures distance to a verified lower bound, not necessarily true optimizer error.\\n+- Paired comparisons on identical targets from cross-ceiling summaries with different attainable cohorts.\\n+- Three sampling seeds from independent training replicates. Public pools and some targets/ancestry may overlap.\\n+\\n+Existing intervals use 200 paired cluster resamples with RNG seed 48271, conditional on fixed snapshots and rival pools. They compare the selected procedure with random or greedy policies, not aggregation rules with each other. Do not reuse those intervals for the central reversal, invent p-values, or call the certification intervals statistical confidence intervals. Show all seed summaries and describe the cross-rule comparison as descriptive.\\n+\\n+Keep matched constant-ceiling, zero-response, permutation, and replay checks in a concise scope discussion; replay has statistical weight zero. Passing them establishes only the tested properties. Report auxiliary six-coordinate projections and revision-matched BBH separately, never pooled into primary scores or described as independent transfer replication.\\n+\\n+## Required figures and layout\\n+\\n+The inspected `paper.sty` declares a **5.5-inch text width and 9-inch text height** in a single-column ICLR layout. Thus `full_width` means the one text column, not a two-column spread. Half-width placement would provide only about 2.75 inches and is unsuitable for the planned multi-panel comparisons. Use ordinary full-text-width figures, not a two-column layout workaround.\\n+\\n+| Figure | Concrete design and source | Readability budget and footprint |\\n+| --- | --- | --- |\\n+| 1. Investment overview | `generate-concept-figure`; fixed scores/rivals, target-only headroom equation, three aggregation branches, exact/infeasible/bounded support outcomes. Source: `final.evidence.episodes`, interpreted with inspected source/contract. No numerical toy result. | One shallow diagram, at most six visual groups and three aggregator branches; approximately 5.5 by 1.8 inches; full width on page 1 or 2; at least 9-point labels. |\\n+| 2. Exact rule contrast | `matplotlib`; two side-by-side signed dot plots at half and full headroom, each showing the per-seed median-minus-mean exact support fraction on the same fixed cohort. Source: ordinary primary Open LLM slices of `final.evidence.episodes`. | Two panels, two per row, three seed categories, one contrast series; approximately 5.5 by 2.1 inches; full width; same signed y scale and zero line; caption gives cohort counts. No invented error bars. |\\n+| 3. Attainability and support scope | `matplotlib`; 2-by-2 composite, rows HELM/Open LLM; left all-target attainment at three ceilings; right paired support bounds at half/full headroom. Source: ordinary primary `final.evidence.episodes`. | Four panels, two per row, at most three categories and three rule series per panel; approximately 5.5 by 3.4 inches; full width, common legend and readable scales; at least 9-point labels. |\\n+\\n+For Figure 3 right panels, intersect attainable targets across all three rules within each seed and ceiling, state cohort sizes, and average the within-seed lower and feasible upper fractions with declared equal seed weights. Unlike Figure 2, these cohorts may differ across ceilings. Exact costs collapse to points; other intervals are certification ranges. Show an empty cohort as not estimable, not as a cost or an imputed value. Do not use these changing-cohort panels alone to establish the central reversal.\\n+\\n+All figures are direct condition comparisons; no optimization trajectories, milestone views, or campaign timelines. Use tables for scope, status counts, and policy differences rather than another dense dashboard. Quantitative figures must export vector PDF and PNG at 300 DPI from source; LaTeX uses PDF whenever available. Preserve editable overview source and prompt provenance. If only raster is available, regenerate at least 2400 pixels wide for full-width placement, or 1200 pixels for a later justified narrow placement; never upscale. Only the overview uses the concept-figure workflow. This stage does not generate figures or invoke that workflow.\\n+\\n+## Main-body budget and venue contract\\n+\\n+Target ICLR 2026, anonymized, with about **8.5 substantive body pages excluding references**. Figure area is included in the following allocation:\\n+\\n+| Scientific use of space | Approximate pages |\\n+| --- | ---: |\\n+| Abstract, introduction, precise contribution and scope | 1.25 |\\n+| Safely grounded related work and modeling context | 0.75 |\\n+| Bounded-response objective and assumptions | 1.00 |\\n+| Support computation and certificate scope | 1.00 |\\n+| Public-panel protocol, pairing and uncertainty | 0.75 |\\n+| Exact contrast, attainment, support bounds and comparators, including figures | 2.75 |\\n+| Limitations and conclusion | 1.00 |\\n+\\n+An eight-page body counts only if its last page is at least 75 percent full. Expand useful model explanation, certificate reasoning, comparison clarity, and limitation analysis before adding visual or textual filler. Do not import the NeurIPS template or checklist obligation from a source-data manifest in place of the selected ICLR venue requirements. Use the provided ICLR style, with no author names, affiliations, identifying links, acknowledgements, or funding statement. Include a separate `LLM Usage` section, optionally after references, describing actual assistance only.\\n+\\n+Suggested headings: **Introduction; Related Work and Scope; Bounded-Response Investment; Computing Support and Certifying Limits; Public Score Panels and Comparison Protocol; Response-Dependent Aggregation Costs; Attainability and Certificate Scope; Limitations and Conclusion.**\\n+\\n+## Supplementary Information after references\\n+\\n+Purpose: add grounded mathematical, uncertainty, sensitivity, and reproduction depth without concealing evidence essential to the thesis. No new experiment or guessed later ranking is required. Route separately supplied authoritative appendix-ranked analyses here without retroactively modifying the strategy.\\n+\\n+| Planned subsection | Available grounded content | Registered source IDs |\\n+| --- | --- | --- |\\n+| Support objective, aggregation conventions, and certificates | Full objective, strict margin, median/trim definitions, headroom argument, enumeration, infeasibility test, conservative-bound and feasible-witness reasoning, tied to inspected frozen source and `task/evaluate_final.py`. | `final.evidence.episodes` |\\n+| Complete rule-by-response and comparator tables | All ordinary primary counts, support/status/bounds, zero/random/greedy comparisons and recorded conditional cluster intervals, including null effects. | `final.evidence.episodes`; `final.metric.feasible_rate`; `final.metric.mean_effort_fraction`; `final.metric.mean_verified_gap_fraction` |\\n+| Task granularity and auxiliary sensitivity | Separate six-task projections and BBH records using evaluator routing, revision reconciliation, and distinct-run caveat; no unrun causal granularity experiment. | `final.evidence.episodes` |\\n+| Matched controls and evaluation scope | Constant/zero-response/permutation/replay checks and their narrow interpretations; completed final qualification and retained evidence-trust caveat. | `final.evidence.episodes`; `final.metric.control_pass_rate`; `final.qualification.status`; `final.qualification.outcome`; `final.qualification.correct` |\\n+| Frozen selection and unsuccessful alternatives | Brief nonchronological disclosure of baseline selection, zero search-score change, three scored and zero unscored attempts; unknown failure causes and search/final separation. | `study.selection_kind`; `study.investigation_outcome`; `study.search_score_delta`; `study.attempts.total`; `study.attempts.scored`; `study.attempts.unscored` |\\n+| Public data provenance and reproduction map | Existing source manifests, hashes, normalization/alias grouping, filtering, strata/seeds, CPU dependencies and commands; planned script-to-table/figure map; license uncertainty and evaluation-setting differences. | `final.evidence.episodes` |\\n+| LLM Usage | Disclose documented ideation, code preparation, query planning, and framing assistance; add writing/figure use only if it actually occurs. Do not invent identities, human checks, or training. | `study.selection_kind`; `study.attempts.total`; `final.evidence.episodes` |\\n+\\n+The listed IDs anchor evaluated outcomes; direct method and provenance details must additionally cite their actual local artifacts in the later evidence map, rather than pretending an episode record itself contains the entire source manifest.\\n+\\n+## Reproducibility and reference handoff\\n+\\n+Use HELM **v1.13.0**, Open LLM contents revision `9c09a7cae43334062a82cb164f2ef255013dafa2`, and the distinct results revision `aa81ecc38fdc5708254b833923368970efdf5ef5`. The final manifest records acquisition on 2026-11-17 and extracted-record SHA-256 `d80abb1b13c6962e15f04d9794fc18fcf39e91cf7c79c679e233d3031f934398`. Preserve each source checksum from `task/resources/final/manifest.json`, and distinguish public repository sizes from the evaluated extracted pools. Existing manifest and raw records support normalization, filtering, alias grouping, split, and setting caveats; do not claim perfectly homogeneous evaluation conditions.\\n+\\n+BBH reconciliation matches model revisions but does not prove identical evaluation settings. In the Open LLM auxiliary routing, odd slots use BBH and even slots use the primary-family projection. Do not match auxiliary slots to primary model identities without reconstructing their actual identifiers. Data-specific redistribution permission remains unresolved: public accessibility, code licenses, and model licenses do not establish a score-data redistribution license.\\n+\\n+The writer must create deterministic derived-data/plot/table scripts, record their exact source slices and commands, and provide the dependency versions already available in `task/requirements.txt`. Those manuscript reproduction scripts are not present merely because the evaluated solver exists. Regeneration from existing records is not a new empirical run; any genuinely new analysis must be labeled and grounded separately.\\n+\\n+The bibliography currently provides metadata retrieval, not evidence of substantive reading, and many entries are tangential. Several relevant starter records are absent. Before literature-dependent prose, curate safely and actually read the permitted source; use only available, verified citation keys and do not fabricate positioning or pad related work. This is a writer-stage prerequisite, not a reason to invent a novelty claim now. No external page was accessed during strategy generation. Do not identify or search for the prohibited study, expand citation graphs, or use discussion/aggregation pages; stop and log any accidental exposure.\\n+\\n+## Language guardrails\\n+\\n+**Forbid headings:** Search Progression; Campaign Phases; Milestones; First Valid Result; Timeline; Experiment A; Experiment B; From Baseline to Winner; Optimization Breakthroughs; Successful Certificate Variants.\\n+\\n+**Forbid phrases:** “we then tried,” “first valid result,” “subsequent improvements,” “next-best,” “later variants,” “winning implementation,” “state of the art,” “universally most robust aggregation,” “median always requires more investment,” “measured training cost,” “causal contamination effect,” and “all full-panel solutions are optimal.”\\n+\\n+Private-only terminology exclusions for manuscript prose: `correctness rate`, `correct and eligible`, `eligible`, `combined_score`, `rubric`, `worker_01`, and `worker_02`. Prefer target attainment rate, support fraction, strict first place, exact minimum support, certified infeasibility, and feasible support interval.\\n+\\n+## Completion boundary\\n+\\n+This strategy supports a coherent conditional scientific paper, not a claim of conference acceptance or an already-complete reproduction package. Core limitations, unsuccessful search disclosure, all-target attainment, conditioning definitions, and exact-versus-bounded scope remain in the main paper. No manuscript, claim-mapping JSON, figure, or new research experiment is produced here, and final-paper validation is not run. Bibliographic substantive reading, plotting scripts, manuscript drafting, and later validation remain downstream work.\\n*** End Patch'\\\"'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n68:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_43\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/sh -lc 'apply_patch() { /usr/local/lib/node_modules/@openai/codex/node_modules/@openai/codex-linux-x64/vendor/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/bin/codex --codex-run-as-apply-patch \\\"$@\\\"; }\\napply_patch '\\\"'*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /workspace/paper/paper_strategy.json\\n+{\\n+  \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"ready\\\\\\\",\\n+  \\\\\\\"selected_prompt_family\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"paper_standalone\\\\\\\",\\n+  \\\\\\\"recommended_title\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Response Ceilings and Targeted Investment in Multitask Leaderboards\\\\\\\",\\n+  \\\\\\\"central_question\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Under a bounded, target-only score-response model with fixed rivals, how many task coordinates must be improved to attain strict first place, and how does that investment depend on the aggregation rule and response ceiling?\\\\\\\",\\n+  \\\\\\\"central_thesis\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"In the evaluated public score panels, aggregation robustness is conditional on the response ceiling: exact six-task results reverse the mean–median minimum-support ordering between half and full headroom on matched attainable targets, while larger subject-level panels establish feasible investment bounds rather than exact rule rankings.\\\\\\\",\\n+  \\\\\\\"narrative_rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"This is a bounded counterfactual empirical study, not a new optimizer or training study. Existing final decision records support a direct rule-by-response comparison, including an exact matched-cohort reversal on the six-task Open LLM panel and explicit uncertainty about optimal support on the 57-subject HELM panel. The same scientific question organizes these as complementary evidence blocks with different certificate strength, not as transfer or discovery-order experiments. The frozen reference procedure is the studied method; unsuccessful search proposals are not the contribution. No universal ordering, practical training cost, or causal contamination effect is inferred.\\\\\\\",\\n+  \\\\\\\"prior_paper_story_status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rejected\\\\\\\",\\n+  \\\\\\\"edit_framing_decision\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No edit context, previous_paper directory, prior manuscript, aggregated directory, or extra_tasks directory is staged. The rejected status denotes rejection of an assumed inherited improvement story, not rejection of an actual manuscript. Compare three alternatives explicitly: preserve an optimizer-improvement story, broaden to a shared novel certificate family, or recenter on response-dependent investment comparisons. Choose the third: no search improvement was selected, component ablations are absent, and exact rule contrasts are stronger than claims of algorithmic novelty.\\\\\\\",\\n+  \\\\\\\"staged_input_impact\\\\\\\": [\\n+    \\\\\\\"Directly inspected source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py and the baseline counterpart; their source files are identical. The selected procedure exhausts panels with at most six coordinates, uses sorted headroom for larger mean panels, and marginal-score greedy supports for larger median and trimmed-mean panels.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Read final_evaluation independently of downstream_study. Its completed, qualified evaluation supports a finished empirical study; it does not establish population generalization or solver novelty.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"The ordinary primary six-task records contain exact support outcomes, whereas the 57-subject median and trimmed-mean records retain bounded support outcomes. This changes the center of gravity from solver improvement to aggregation sensitivity with explicit certificate scope.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"The separate auxiliary BBH and six-coordinate projections add sensitivity and verification depth, not a new architecture, new model training condition, or a pooled primary benchmark.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"The local ICLR style is single-column, with a 5.5-inch text width and 9-inch text height. This supports full-text-width, low-density comparisons rather than two-column dashboard figures.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"The supplied bibliography contains metadata retrieval records, many tangential to this study, without evidence of substantive reading. Its presence does not license scientific positioning or citation padding. No external source was accessed during strategy generation.\\\\\\\"\\n+  ],\\n+  \\\\\\\"method_groups\\\\\\\": [\\n+    {\\n+      \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Frozen bounded-headroom support-minimization procedure\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"role\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"supporting\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"include_reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"This is the selected studied procedure, not a newly successful proposal: improve selected coordinates by alpha times their remaining headroom, hold rivals fixed, and report exact support, certified infeasibility, or an honest lower–upper support interval. Explain exhaustive small-panel search, exact mean sorting, and larger-panel greedy witnesses separately.\\\\\\\"\\n+    },\\n+    {\\n+      \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Equal-task arithmetic mean\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"role\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"baseline\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"include_reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Provides the directly grounded aggregation comparator and an analytically exact sorted-headroom solution; retain it in every main rule comparison.\\\\\\\"\\n+    },\\n+    {\\n+      \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Conventional median\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"role\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"supporting\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"include_reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The central exact six-task contrast uses the conventional median, including the average of the two middle values for an even task count; distinguish this from a lower or upper median.\\\\\\\"\\n+    },\\n+    {\\n+      \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Symmetric 20-percent trimmed mean\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"role\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"supporting\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"include_reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Provides the grounded intermediate order-statistic condition: remove floor(m/5) values from each tail. It checks whether the evidence is specific to the median without extending to untested ordinal rules.\\\\\\\"\\n+    },\\n+    {\\n+      \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No-intervention, seeded-random, and marginal-score-greedy investment policies\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"role\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"baseline\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"include_reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"These comparators already have matched final decision records. They contextualize support selection, retain zero and negative differences, and show that the selected procedure coincides with greedy in important regimes. They are not component ablations or independent model-training methods.\\\\\\\"\\n+    }\\n+  ],\\n+  \\\\\\\"results_focus\\\\\\\": [\\n+    \\\\\\\"Primary thesis test: ordinary Open LLM primary decisions only; match by seed and target slot and retain targets attainable under both mean and median at alpha=0.5 and alpha=1.0. Compare exact support fractions on that identical per-seed cohort across both response conditions. The recorded data give a negative median-minus-mean average at half headroom and a positive average at full headroom for every final seed. This is a descriptive within-snapshot reversal, not a pre-registered significance claim.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Report attainability for all sampled ordinary primary targets at alpha=0.25, 0.5, and 1.0, separately for HELM and Open LLM, so conditioning the exact contrast on attainable cases cannot conceal infeasible targets.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Report support cost with exactness attached: exact support for the six-task panel and the mean, but evaluator lower bounds and selected feasible upper bounds for larger median/trimmed panels. A reversal of greedy witness costs on HELM must not be called a reversal of minimum costs when bound intervals overlap.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Retain matched policy comparisons, preferably a compact main table at alpha=0.5 and the complete grid after references. State where exact selection reduces support relative to greedy and where it ties. Existing paired intervals compare the selected procedure against random or greedy; they are not cross-rule confidence intervals.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Keep constant-ceiling, zero-response, permutation, and replay checks separate from ordinary performance. A passed check establishes only the property tested, not universal scientific validity or optimality.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Use auxiliary six-coordinate projections and revision-matched BBH decisions only as separately labeled sensitivity evidence. Do not merge them with primary scores, compare their target slots as identical model identities, or claim domain transfer.\\\\\\\"\\n+  ],\\n+  \\\\\\\"figure_plan\\\\\\\": [\\n+    \\\\\\\"Figure 1, early overview: fixed public task scores and rivals; target-only bounded-headroom intervention; three aggregation rules leading to exact support, infeasibility, or an interval. No fabricated score matrix or illustrative numerical result.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Figure 2, central exact comparison: two matched-cohort dot plots, one for half headroom and one for full headroom, showing median-minus-mean minimum-support fraction by final sampling seed with a zero reference line.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Figure 3, scope and cost: a 2-by-2 composite with one row per primary panel family, all-target attainability at three response ceilings on the left, and paired attainable-cohort support bounds at half/full headroom on the right. Exact values and unresolved intervals use visibly different marks.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Use tables, not additional main figures, for snapshot scope, comparator differences, and certificate/status counts. Put the full conditional comparator-interval grid and auxiliary sensitivities after references.\\\\\\\"\\n+  ],\\n+  \\\\\\\"figure_specs\\\\\\\": [\\n+    {\\n+      \\\\\\\"figure_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"investment_overview\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"required\\\\\\\": true,\\n+      \\\\\\\"purpose\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Make the counterfactual investment object, fixed-rival assumption, aggregation conditions, and certificate outcomes legible before quantitative results.\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"figure_type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"diagram\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"preferred_generator\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"generate-concept-figure\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"group_by\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"score intervention and certificate scope\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"metric\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"none; qualitative specification only\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"split_by\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"fixed scores, bounded intervention, aggregation and support outcome\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"preferred_span\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"full_width\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"target_width_fraction\\\\\\\": 1.0,\\n+      \\\\\\\"layout_rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"In the inspected single-column ICLR style, full width is 5.5 inches, not a two-column spread. Use a shallow approximately 5.5-by-1.8-inch diagram on page 1 or 2; a half-width 2.75-inch rendering would compress the update equation and outcome labels. Keep at most six visual groups and three aggregator branches, with at least 9-point rendered labels.\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"allow_progression\\\\\\\": false,\\n+      \\\\\\\"max_panels\\\\\\\": 1,\\n+      \\\\\\\"max_panels_per_row\\\\\\\": 1,\\n+      \\\\\\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\\\\\": 6,\\n+      \\\\\\\"max_series_per_panel\\\\\\\": 3,\\n+      \\\\\\\"source_ids\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\\\\\"],\\n+      \\\\\\\"content_constraints\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Show x_j changing to x_j+alpha(1-x_j) only on the selected support and label rivals fixed. Three aggregators are conditions, not sequential improvements. Distinguish exact, infeasible, and bounded outcomes. Do not draw training, an architecture transition, a novel certificate mechanism, or numerical toy measurements.\\\\\\\"\\n+    },\\n+    {\\n+      \\\\\\\"figure_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"exact_rule_contrast\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"required\\\\\\\": true,\\n+      \\\\\\\"purpose\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Display the exact within-snapshot mean–median ordering reversal without infeasibility penalties, composition changes across response conditions, or search chronology.\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"figure_type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"paired_difference_dotplot\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"preferred_generator\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"matplotlib\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"group_by\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"final sampling seed\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"metric\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"mean exact median-minus-mean support fraction on a fixed jointly attainable cohort\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"split_by\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"alpha=0.5 versus alpha=1.0 on the ordinary Open LLM primary panel\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"preferred_span\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"full_width\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"target_width_fraction\\\\\\\": 1.0,\\n+      \\\\\\\"layout_rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Two side-by-side panels occupy approximately 5.5 by 2.1 inches in the 5.5-inch single text column. Each panel has three seed categories and one contrast series, so 9-point labels and a common signed y scale remain readable; include a horizontal zero line and cohort counts in the caption. Do not connect response conditions as a time trajectory.\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"allow_progression\\\\\\\": false,\\n+      \\\\\\\"max_panels\\\\\\\": 2,\\n+      \\\\\\\"max_panels_per_row\\\\\\\": 2,\\n+      \\\\\\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\\\\\": 3,\\n+      \\\\\\\"max_series_per_panel\\\\\\\": 1,\\n+      \\\\\\\"source_ids\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\\\\\"],\\n+      \\\\\\\"content_constraints\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Filter ordinary primary Open LLM decisions, join rule/alpha cells by seed and slot, and intersect attainability under both rules at both response conditions. Each seed retains the same cohort in both panels. Plot exact support-count differences divided by six; show individual seed summaries, not invented confidence intervals or a pooled population p-value.\\\\\\\"\\n+    },\\n+    {\\n+      \\\\\\\"figure_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"attainability_and_support_scope\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"required\\\\\\\": true,\\n+      \\\\\\\"purpose\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Show which targets can attain first place and how much support is established, while exposing differences between exact and bounded evidence.\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"figure_type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"attainment_points_and_support_intervals\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"preferred_generator\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"matplotlib\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"group_by\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"aggregation rule\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"metric\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"left: target attainment rate; right: normalized support lower and feasible upper bounds\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"split_by\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"HELM 57-subject panel versus Open LLM six-task panel\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"preferred_span\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"full_width\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"target_width_fraction\\\\\\\": 1.0,\\n+      \\\\\\\"layout_rationale\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"A 2-by-2 figure at approximately 5.5 by 3.4 inches uses the full single-column width. Two panels per row, three ceiling categories at most, three rule series, shared scales, and a common legend avoid shrinking a dashboard. Use at least 9-point final labels and a short caption explicitly defining the support cohorts and interval semantics.\\\\\\\",\\n+      \\\\\\\"allow_progression\\\\\\\": false,\\n+      \\\\\\\"max_panels\\\\\\\": 4,\\n+      \\\\\\\"max_panels_per_row\\\\\\\": 2,\\n+      \\\\\\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\\\\\": 3,\\n+      \\\\\\\"max_series_per_panel\\\\\\\": 3,\\n+      \\\\\\\"source_ids\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\\\\\"],\\n+      \\\\\\\"content_constraints\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Left panels include every ordinary primary target at all three recorded ceilings and use one attainment definition: a verified strict-first support with a supported claim. Right panels use only alpha=0.5 and 1.0, intersect attainable targets across all three rules within each seed and ceiling, and report the cohort sizes. Average the within-seed lower and upper support fractions with declared equal seed weights; the interval is an identification/certification range, not a confidence interval. Cohorts here may differ across ceilings, unlike Figure 2. Exact costs collapse to points. Never draw the infeasible sentinel m+1 as an actual cost. If a required joint cohort is empty, show not estimable rather than imputation.\\\\\\\"\\n+    }\\n+  ],\\n+  \\\\\\\"supplementary_plan\\\\\\\": {\\n+    \\\\\\\"purpose\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Provide substantive mathematical, conditional-uncertainty, sensitivity, and reproducibility depth after references without hiding the central exact contrast, unattainability, or larger-panel certification limits from the main body.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"planned_subsections\\\\\\\": [\\n+      {\\n+        \\\\\\\"heading\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Support objective, aggregation conventions, and certificates\\\\\\\",\\n+        \\\\\\\"grounded_content\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Give the complete target-only objective, strict-first tolerance, even median and trimming conventions, mean sorted-headroom argument, exhaustive six-coordinate procedure, full-uplift infeasibility test, and the conservative lower-bound versus feasible-witness distinction. Tie explanations to the inspected frozen source and task/evaluate_final.py; do not describe abandoned bounds as evaluated contributions.\\\\\\\",\\n+        \\\\\\\"source_ids\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\\\\\"]\\n+      },\\n+      {\\n+        \\\\\\\"heading\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Complete rule-by-response and comparator tables\\\\\\\",\\n+        \\\\\\\"grounded_content\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Tabulate ordinary primary decisions by family, seed, rule, and ceiling, retaining attainment counts, exact/interval status, lower bounds, feasible support sizes, and all zero/random/greedy references. Include the already-recorded per-seed cluster-percentile intervals for selected-minus-random and selected-minus-greedy effort, their conditional scope and all null effects; do not reinterpret them as cross-rule inference.\\\\\\\",\\n+        \\\\\\\"source_ids\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"final.metric.feasible_rate\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"final.metric.mean_effort_fraction\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"final.metric.mean_verified_gap_fraction\\\\\\\"]\\n+      },\\n+      {\\n+        \\\\\\\"heading\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Task granularity and auxiliary sensitivity\\\\\\\",\\n+        \\\\\\\"grounded_content\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Separate auxiliary six-task projections from the BBH subtask subset using family, panel, and slot routing in task/evaluate_final.py. Report the already-recorded auxiliary outcomes, revision reconciliation, and distinct evaluation-setting caveat. No new resampling experiment, unrun ablation, or causal granularity attribution is promised.\\\\\\\",\\n+        \\\\\\\"source_ids\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\\\\\"]\\n+      },\\n+      {\\n+        \\\\\\\"heading\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Matched controls and evaluation scope\\\\\\\",\\n+        \\\\\\\"grounded_content\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Describe constant-ceiling, zero-response, column-permutation and reset-replay checks, including replay statistical weight zero. Report the completed final qualification faithfully and explain that it does not prove every minimum-support statement or independent benchmark generalization. Retain the evidence trust limitation rather than promoting candidate diagnostics into verified facts.\\\\\\\",\\n+        \\\\\\\"source_ids\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"final.metric.control_pass_rate\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"final.qualification.status\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"final.qualification.outcome\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"final.qualification.correct\\\\\\\"]\\n+      },\\n+      {\\n+        \\\\\\\"heading\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Frozen selection and unsuccessful alternatives\\\\\\\",\\n+        \\\\\\\"grounded_content\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Provide a concise nonchronological disclosure of baseline selection, zero search-score change, three scored alternatives, and zero unscored alternatives. None was a qualifying search winner. Report unsuccessful outcomes without inventing a defect, adaptivity explanation, or measured loss for absent evidence; keep search quantities separate from final measurements.\\\\\\\",\\n+        \\\\\\\"source_ids\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"study.selection_kind\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"study.investigation_outcome\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"study.search_score_delta\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"study.attempts.total\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"study.attempts.scored\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"study.attempts.unscored\\\\\\\"]\\n+      },\\n+      {\\n+        \\\\\\\"heading\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Public data provenance and reproduction map\\\\\\\",\\n+        \\\\\\\"grounded_content\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Use existing source records and manifest to document HELM release, the two pinned Open LLM revisions, acquisition time, source and extracted-record hashes, normalization, alias grouping, filtering, target strata, seeds, dependency versions, and CPU commands. Map every eventual plot/table to its derived-data script and source slice; mark those scripts as a writer-stage deliverable, not already present. State unresolved score-data redistribution licensing and variable evaluation settings.\\\\\\\",\\n+        \\\\\\\"source_ids\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\\\\\"]\\n+      },\\n+      {\\n+        \\\\\\\"heading\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"LLM Usage\\\\\\\",\\n+        \\\\\\\"grounded_content\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Disclose the documented LLM role in research ideation, code preparation, reference-query planning, and manuscript framing; add writing/figure assistance only when actually used. State that counterfactual score edits are not model training. Do not invent model identities, provider details, human validation, or a literature-exposure history.\\\\\\\",\\n+        \\\\\\\"source_ids\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"study.selection_kind\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"study.attempts.total\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\\\\\"]\\n+      }\\n+    ]\\n+  },\\n+  \\\\\\\"forbidden_headings\\\\\\\": [\\n+    \\\\\\\"Search Progression\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Campaign Phases\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Milestones\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"First Valid Result\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Timeline\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Experiment A\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Experiment B\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"From Baseline to Winner\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Optimization Breakthroughs\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Successful Certificate Variants\\\\\\\"\\n+  ],\\n+  \\\\\\\"forbidden_phrases\\\\\\\": [\\n+    \\\\\\\"we then tried\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"first valid result\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"subsequent improvements\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"next-best\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"later variants\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"winning implementation\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"state of the art\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"universally most robust aggregation\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"median always requires more investment\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"measured training cost\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"causal contamination effect\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"all full-panel solutions are optimal\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"correctness rate\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"correct and eligible\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"eligible\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"combined_score\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"rubric\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"worker_01\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"worker_02\\\\\\\"\\n+  ],\\n+  \\\\\\\"notes_for_writer\\\\\\\": [\\n+    \\\\\\\"Format contract: target the provided ICLR 2026 single-column style and anonymized review format. The inspected paper.sty declares textwidth 5.5in and textheight 9in. Here preferred_span=full_width means the one full text column; a column-width two-column convention does not apply. Do not replace the venue with the NeurIPS template mentioned in source-task provenance.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Body plan: aim for about 8.5 substantive pages, excluding references: 1.25 pages for abstract/introduction and contribution scope, 0.75 for safely grounded related work and modeling context, 1.0 for objective/assumptions, 1.0 for solver and certificate scope, 0.75 for experimental protocol and uncertainty, 2.75 for exact contrast/attainability/support/comparators including figures, and 1.0 for limitations and conclusion. Figure area is included, not added on top. An eight-page body must fill at least 75 percent of its last page; never pad to reach this threshold.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Suggested thesis-first headings: Introduction; Related Work and Scope; Bounded-Response Investment; Computing Support and Certifying Limits; Public Score Panels and Comparison Protocol; Response-Dependent Aggregation Costs; Attainability and Certificate Scope; Limitations and Conclusion. No campaign-order sections.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Define x in [0,1], selected support S, target update x_j+alpha(1-x_j) for j in S, fixed competitors, and unique first as aggregate(target)>max rival aggregate+1e-10. Investment is |S|, normalized by panel task count for cross-panel display. Total normalized score lift is secondary and is not training examples, compute, dollars, or contamination severity. Alpha is a stipulated response fraction, not an estimated learning curve.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"State equal task weighting, no spillover or regression on untouched coordinates, fixed rival pool, and score normalization explicitly. A support-cardinality comparison across six tasks and 57 subjects does not equate their real-world intervention costs. Avoid interpreting named architectures or task metadata as controlled architecture experiments.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Private-only grounding audit: final.qualification.status=completed, final.qualification.outcome=qualified, and final.qualification.correct=true are authoritative for final qualification, read independently from study.final.*. Preserve this assessment during writing, review, audit, and revision; if later authoritative qualification differs, disclose failure and limitations rather than keeping this positive label. Qualification is neither a novelty certificate nor generalization evidence.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Private-only selection audit: study.selection_kind=baseline, study.investigation_outcome=completed_no_winner, study.search_score_delta=0, study.attempts.scored=3 and study.attempts.unscored=0. The frozen source equals the original baseline source. Keep search scores and final scores in their separate scopes. Failed alternatives have no grounded failure-cause diagnosis; do not choose between performance, validity, or adaptivity explanations without additional evaluator evidence.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Private-only final evidence audit: final.evidence.episodes is the quantitative source for every planned rule-specific comparison and recorded paired interval. It contains final seeds 1009, 1013, and 1019. Its candidate_diagnostics_trust is unverified. The source file checksum matches the manifest, and the final evaluator computes witness checks and small-panel audits, but do not promote any unverified candidate diagnostic or the exact_audit_pass field alone into a universal exactness claim. Attach explicit source slices and evaluator conventions to every derived result.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Private-only descriptive cohort check, derived from existing final records, not a new experiment: Figure 2 retains 18, 17, and 17 targets for seeds 1009, 1013, and 1019. Median-minus-mean support-fraction averages are respectively -0.129630, -0.127451, -0.068627 at alpha=0.5 and +0.138889, +0.127451, +0.156863 at alpha=1.0. Recompute from selected support counts in the plotting script rather than hard-coding these rounded audit values. This subset analysis is descriptive and was chosen during framing.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Private-only metric semantics: final.metric.mean_effort_fraction uses a value of one for nonattainment, so it is a penalized summary, not the mean minimum investment of successful targets. final.metric.mean_verified_gap_fraction is relative to a verified lower bound and is not necessarily true optimizer error. Do not use these aggregates as substitutes for the paired cohort analysis or mix control cases into ordinary-result plots.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Uncertainty contract: final sampling seeds reuse fixed public panels and may share targets or model ancestry; they are not independent training replicates. Existing paired intervals use 200 cluster resamples with RNG seed 48271 and are conditional on fixed snapshots/rival pools. Keep all three seed summaries visible or tabulated. No existing cross-rule interval or p-value supports the reversal, and baseline intervals cannot be reassigned to it.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Main tables: a compact scope table distinguishing public source snapshots from the evaluated extracted panels; an investment/certificate table with cohort sizes and infeasible counts; and a matched policy-difference table at alpha=0.5 for both families and all three rules. Include ties with greedy; put the complete already-recorded interval grid after references. These are planned transformations of existing records, not unperformed experiments.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"The main body must retain the exact six-task comparison, unconditional attainment rates, conditioning definitions, larger-panel interval caveat, uncertainty scope, and failed-search disclosure in brief. Supplementary material expands them; it must not hide contradictory or essential evidence. Route any separately supplied authoritative appendix-ranked analyses after references without inventing a ranking or retroactively changing this strategy.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Provenance contract: HELM v1.13.0; Open LLM contents revision 9c09a7cae43334062a82cb164f2ef255013dafa2; separate results revision aa81ecc38fdc5708254b833923368970efdf5ef5. The final manifest records acquisition on 2026-11-17 and extracted records SHA-256 d80abb1b13c6962e15f04d9794fc18fcf39e91cf7c79c679e233d3031f934398. Use task/resources/final/manifest.json and records.json for source/normalization/license details. Do not claim evaluation of every row in the public repositories.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"BBH scope: the existing manifest records model-revision reconciliation but explicitly says contents and results are distinct runs with potentially different settings. Auxiliary Open LLM odd slots route to BBH and even slots to the primary-family projection. Use the routing code to separate them, not the generic auxiliary label alone. BBH is not an independent replicated transfer benchmark.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Literature contract: cite only existing bibliography keys after safely reading the actual permitted source; retrieval metadata is not substantive reading. Many supplied entries are tangential, and several relevant starter records are absent, so bibliography curation and safe substantive reading remain writer-stage prerequisites before related-work claims. Do not fill space with unrelated citations or claim novelty against unread papers. Never search for the prohibited study, expand citation graphs, or infer its identity; log and stop any accidental exposure.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Figure production contract: only the overview uses generate-concept-figure, retaining editable source and prompt provenance. This stage plans figures and does not run that workflow. Quantitative figures must be script-generated vector PDF plus 300-DPI PNG; use the PDF in LaTeX whenever it exists. For a raster-only overview, regenerate at at least 2400 pixels wide at full width, or at least 1200 pixels if a later justified column-width placement is chosen; never upscale. Keep rendered labels at least 9pt and simplify rather than shrinking dense figures.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Keep artifact and internal decision terminology private. Reader-facing terms are target attainment rate, support fraction, strict first place, exact minimum support, certified infeasibility, and feasible support interval. Do not turn the selected reference into a novel learned method, or experimental controls into scientific success rates.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"Required separate LLM Usage disclosure belongs after references if needed; remove names, affiliations, acknowledgements, funding statements, and identifying repository links. Describe only actual assistance documented in run artifacts. Do not claim human checks, literature reading, or training that did not occur.\\\\\\\",\\n+    \\\\\\\"This strategy creates neither a manuscript nor claim-mapping artifacts, generates no figures, performs no new research experiment, and does not run final-paper validation. A ready framing is not a claim that manuscript reproduction scripts, substantive citation verification, or a compiled paper already exist.\\\\\\\"\\n+  ],\\n+  \\\\\\\"failure_reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\n+}\\n*** Add File: /workspace/paper/paper_strategy.md\\n+# Paper strategy: response ceilings and targeted investment\\n+\\n+**Status:** ready. **Prompt family:** \\\"'`paper_standalone` / `write-paper-standalone`.\\n+**Provisional title:** Response Ceilings and Targeted Investment in Multitask Leaderboards.\\n+\\n+## Scientific center\\n+\\n+**Question.** Under a bounded, target-only score-response model with fixed rivals, how many task coordinates must be improved to attain strict first place, and how does that investment depend on the aggregation rule and response ceiling?\\n+\\n+**Thesis.** In the evaluated public score panels, aggregation robustness is conditional on the response ceiling: exact six-task results reverse the mean–median minimum-support ordering between half and full headroom on matched attainable targets, while larger subject-level panels establish feasible investment bounds rather than exact rule rankings.\\n+\\n+This is a standalone conditional empirical study, not an optimizer breakthrough, a training experiment, or a search report. Organize the six-task and subject-level panels as complementary evidence blocks under one question. Their certificate strength differs; neither is evidence of architecture change or domain transfer. The contribution is the precisely defined investment comparison and its measured limits, not a claim that familiar enumeration or greedy selection is new.\\n+\\n+## Framing decision and rejected alternatives\\n+\\n+No edit-context file, previous manuscript, `previous_paper/`, `aggregated/`, or `extra_tasks/` is staged. The JSON status `prior_paper_story_status: rejected` rejects an assumed inherited improvement narrative; there is no actual prior manuscript to reject.\\n+\\n+| Candidate framing | Decision and grounded reason |\\n+| --- | --- |\\n+| Preserve an optimizer-improvement story | Reject: the frozen selection is the reference baseline, not a successful new optimizer. |\\n+| Broaden to a shared novel certificate family | Reject: no component ablations substantiate the abandoned proposal mechanisms, and large-panel median/trimmed costs are not exact. |\\n+| Recenter on response-dependent investment | Choose: final ordinary decision records support direct rule-by-ceiling comparisons, including exact paired contrasts and explicit unattainability. |\\n+\\n+Direct inspection confirms that the staged selected and baseline source files are identical. Their small-panel enumeration, exact mean sorting, and larger-panel greedy witnesses determine what can be claimed. The auxiliary projections and BBH records provide additional scope checks, not a reason to broaden the thesis to a new method family. The venue changes presentation, not the scientific conclusion.\\n+\\n+## Private grounding and qualification audit\\n+\\n+This section is a provenance memo, not manuscript prose. Use these registered source identifiers in downstream claim mapping:\\n+\\n+- `final.qualification.status = completed`, `final.qualification.outcome = qualified`, and `final.qualification.correct = true`. These come from `paper_data.json.final_evaluation`, read independently of selection metadata. Qualification does not establish novelty, population generalization, or every support minimum.\\n+- `study.selection_kind = baseline`; `study.investigation_outcome = completed_no_winner`; `study.search_score_delta = 0`; `study.attempts.scored = 3`; `study.attempts.unscored = 0`. Search evidence and final measurements have distinct scopes. No search alternative has an established qualifying improvement. Missing performance evidence would not be a measured loss.\\n+- `final.evidence.episodes` contains three sampling seeds, ordinary and matched-control cases, primary and auxiliary decisions, and policy-comparison intervals. Its `candidate_diagnostics_trust` remains `unverified`. The evidence-file SHA-256 agrees with the manifest. Direct evaluator inspection shows witness verification and exhaustive small-panel reference computation; that does not license unrelated candidate diagnostics. The field `exact_audit_pass` alone is not proof of full-panel exactness.\\n+- Preserve the final qualification assessment through writing, review, audit, and revision. If authoritative later evidence changes it to a failure, disclose that failure explicitly and retain its limitations. Failed search alternatives have no established causal diagnosis: do not infer performance-only, validity, or adaptivity failure from a boolean outcome.\\n+\\n+The cross-rule cohort check was a read-only summary of existing records, not a new experiment. Restrict to ordinary primary Open LLM decisions and join on seed and target slot. Intersect targets attainable under both mean and median at both half and full headroom. The resulting fixed cohorts contain 18, 17, and 17 targets for seeds 1009, 1013, and 1019. The following rounded values are audit checks derived from `final.evidence.episodes`, not hard-coded plotting inputs:\\n+\\n+| Sampling seed | Median minus mean support fraction, half headroom | Same contrast, full headroom |\\n+| --- | ---: | ---: |\\n+| 1009 | -0.129630 | +0.138889 |\\n+| 1013 | -0.127451 | +0.127451 |\\n+| 1019 | -0.068627 | +0.156863 |\\n+\\n+All feasible primary six-task costs in this contrast have exact support status and correspond to the frozen exhaustive procedure. The reversal is a descriptive within-snapshot result selected during framing, not a preregistered significance finding. Larger-panel HELM witness-cost reversals are not minimum-cost reversals when certification intervals overlap.\\n+\\n+## Scope and method groups\\n+\\n+Define scores in `[0,1]`, a target model, a fixed rival pool, a task panel of size `m`, and selected support `S`. Only selected coordinates change, by `x_j -> x_j + alpha(1-x_j)`, with recorded `alpha` values `0.25`, `0.5`, and `1.0`. Unique first means target aggregate exceeds the largest rival aggregate by more than `1e-10`. Investment is `|S|`, with `|S|/m` used for normalized display. Total normalized score lift is secondary, not dollars, training examples, or compute.\\n+\\n+Include only these method groups:\\n+\\n+1. **Frozen support-minimization procedure — supporting.** Exhaust at most six coordinates, sort headroom for larger means, and construct marginal-score-greedy supports for larger median/trimmed panels. Explain the all-coordinate infeasibility test and exact versus lower–upper outcomes.\\n+2. **Equal-task arithmetic mean — aggregation baseline.** Retain throughout; the headroom solution is exact.\\n+3. **Conventional median — supporting condition.** Average the two middle scores on even panels; do not substitute a different median convention.\\n+4. **Symmetric 20-percent trimmed mean — supporting condition.** Remove `floor(m/5)` scores from each tail.\\n+5. **No-intervention, seeded-random, and marginal-score-greedy policies — selection baselines.** Keep matched recorded comparisons, including ties. They are not component ablations.\\n+\\n+Do not require discarded rank-window or clipped-envelope branches in the main narrative. No evaluated Borda condition, equilibrium model, measured training response, architecture intervention, or unrun ablation belongs in this paper. State equal task weights, no spillover, no score regression outside the support, fixed rivals, and uncertain mapping from score uplift to actual training investment.\\n+\\n+## Results structure and uncertainty\\n+\\n+Lead with the exact fixed-cohort mean–median contrast. Follow it with all-target attainability and support/certificate scope for both primary families. Maintain one definition of **target attainment rate**: the fraction of ordinary primary target decisions with a verified strict-first support and a supported claim. Do not mix controls into that rate.\\n+\\n+Use a compact main comparator table at half headroom for both families and all three rules, retaining ties with greedy and comparisons against random and no intervention. The complete rule/ceiling/seed grid and all recorded comparator intervals belong after references. A meaningful exact-selection advantage in one small-panel condition does not make the frozen reference a newly invented optimizer.\\n+\\n+The main body must distinguish:\\n+\\n+- Exact six-task and mean minimum costs from larger median/trimmed feasible upper bounds and verified lower bounds.\\n+- Unattainable cases from unresolved support intervals. Never draw the `m+1` infeasibility sentinel as an actual intervention cost.\\n+- Successful-target support from a penalized effort summary: `final.metric.mean_effort_fraction` assigns one to nonattainment. Likewise, `final.metric.mean_verified_gap_fraction` measures distance to a verified lower bound, not necessarily true optimizer error.\\n+- Paired comparisons on identical targets from cross-ceiling summaries with different attainable cohorts.\\n+- Three sampling seeds from independent training replicates. Public pools and some targets/ancestry may overlap.\\n+\\n+Existing intervals use 200 paired cluster resamples with RNG seed 48271, conditional on fixed snapshots and rival pools. They compare the selected procedure with random or greedy policies, not aggregation rules with each other. Do not reuse those intervals for the central reversal, invent p-values, or call the certification intervals statistical confidence intervals. Show all seed summaries and describe the cross-rule comparison as descriptive.\\n+\\n+Keep matched constant-ceiling, zero-response, permutation, and replay checks in a concise scope discussion; replay has statistical weight zero. Passing them establishes only the tested properties. Report auxiliary six-coordinate projections and revision-matched BBH separately, never pooled into primary scores or described as independent transfer replication.\\n+\\n+## Required figures and layout\\n+\\n+The inspected `paper.sty` declares a **5.5-inch text width and 9-inch text height** in a single-column ICLR layout. Thus `full_width` means the one text column, not a two-column spread. Half-width placement would provide only about 2.75 inches and is unsuitable for the planned multi-panel comparisons. Use ordinary full-text-width figures, not a two-column layout workaround.\\n+\\n+| Figure | Concrete design and source | Readability budget and footprint |\\n+| --- | --- | --- |\\n+| 1. Investment overview | `generate-concept-figure`; fixed scores/rivals, target-only headroom equation, three aggregation branches, exact/infeasible/bounded support outcomes. Source: `final.evidence.episodes`, interpreted with inspected source/contract. No numerical toy result. | One shallow diagram, at most six visual groups and three aggregator branches; approximately 5.5 by 1.8 inches; full width on page 1 or 2; at least 9-point labels. |\\n+| 2. Exact rule contrast | `matplotlib`; two side-by-side signed dot plots at half and full headroom, each showing the per-seed median-minus-mean exact support fraction on the same fixed cohort. Source: ordinary primary Open LLM slices of `final.evidence.episodes`. | Two panels, two per row, three seed categories, one contrast series; approximately 5.5 by 2.1 inches; full width; same signed y scale and zero line; caption gives cohort counts. No invented error bars. |\\n+| 3. Attainability and support scope | `matplotlib`; 2-by-2 composite, rows HELM/Open LLM; left all-target attainment at three ceilings; right paired support bounds at half/full headroom. Source: ordinary primary `final.evidence.episodes`. | Four panels, two per row, at most three categories and three rule series per panel; approximately 5.5 by 3.4 inches; full width, common legend and readable scales; at least 9-point labels. |\\n+\\n+For Figure 3 right panels, intersect attainable targets across all three rules within each seed and ceiling, state cohort sizes, and average the within-seed lower and feasible upper fractions with declared equal seed weights. Unlike Figure 2, these cohorts may differ across ceilings. Exact costs collapse to points; other intervals are certification ranges. Show an empty cohort as not estimable, not as a cost or an imputed value. Do not use these changing-cohort panels alone to establish the central reversal.\\n+\\n+All figures are direct condition comparisons; no optimization trajectories, milestone views, or campaign timelines. Use tables for scope, status counts, and policy differences rather than another dense dashboard. Quantitative figures must export vector PDF and PNG at 300 DPI from source; LaTeX uses PDF whenever available. Preserve editable overview source and prompt provenance. If only raster is available, regenerate at least 2400 pixels wide for full-width placement, or 1200 pixels for a later justified narrow placement; never upscale. Only the overview uses the concept-figure workflow. This stage does not generate figures or invoke that workflow.\\n+\\n+## Main-body budget and venue contract\\n+\\n+Target ICLR 2026, anonymized, with about **8.5 substantive body pages excluding references**. Figure area is included in the following allocation:\\n+\\n+| Scientific use of space | Approximate pages |\\n+| --- | ---: |\\n+| Abstract, introduction, precise contribution and scope | 1.25 |\\n+| Safely grounded related work and modeling context | 0.75 |\\n+| Bounded-response objective and assumptions | 1.00 |\\n+| Support computation and certificate scope | 1.00 |\\n+| Public-panel protocol, pairing and uncertainty | 0.75 |\\n+| Exact contrast, attainment, support bounds and comparators, including figures | 2.75 |\\n+| Limitations and conclusion | 1.00 |\\n+\\n+An eight-page body counts only if its last page is at least 75 percent full. Expand useful model explanation, certificate reasoning, comparison clarity, and limitation analysis before adding visual or textual filler. Do not import the NeurIPS template or checklist obligation from a source-data manifest in place of the selected ICLR venue requirements. Use the provided ICLR style, with no author names, affiliations, identifying links, acknowledgements, or funding statement. Include a separate `LLM Usage` section, optionally after references, describing actual assistance only.\\n+\\n+Suggested headings: **Introduction; Related Work and Scope; Bounded-Response Investment; Computing Support and Certifying Limits; Public Score Panels and Comparison Protocol; Response-Dependent Aggregation Costs; Attainability and Certificate Scope; Limitations and Conclusion.**\\n+\\n+## Supplementary Information after references\\n+\\n+Purpose: add grounded mathematical, uncertainty, sensitivity, and reproduction depth without concealing evidence essential to the thesis. No new experiment or guessed later ranking is required. Route separately supplied authoritative appendix-ranked analyses here without retroactively modifying the strategy.\\n+\\n+| Planned subsection | Available grounded content | Registered source IDs |\\n+| --- | --- | --- |\\n+| Support objective, aggregation conventions, and certificates | Full objective, strict margin, median/trim definitions, headroom argument, enumeration, infeasibility test, conservative-bound and feasible-witness reasoning, tied to inspected frozen source and `task/evaluate_final.py`. | `final.evidence.episodes` |\\n+| Complete rule-by-response and comparator tables | All ordinary primary counts, support/status/bounds, zero/random/greedy comparisons and recorded conditional cluster intervals, including null effects. | `final.evidence.episodes`; `final.metric.feasible_rate`; `final.metric.mean_effort_fraction`; `final.metric.mean_verified_gap_fraction` |\\n+| Task granularity and auxiliary sensitivity | Separate six-task projections and BBH records using evaluator routing, revision reconciliation, and distinct-run caveat; no unrun causal granularity experiment. | `final.evidence.episodes` |\\n+| Matched controls and evaluation scope | Constant/zero-response/permutation/replay checks and their narrow interpretations; completed final qualification and retained evidence-trust caveat. | `final.evidence.episodes`; `final.metric.control_pass_rate`; `final.qualification.status`; `final.qualification.outcome`; `final.qualification.correct` |\\n+| Frozen selection and unsuccessful alternatives | Brief nonchronological disclosure of baseline selection, zero search-score change, three scored and zero unscored attempts; unknown failure causes and search/final separation. | `study.selection_kind`; `study.investigation_outcome`; `study.search_score_delta`; `study.attempts.total`; `study.attempts.scored`; `study.attempts.unscored` |\\n+| Public data provenance and reproduction map | Existing source manifests, hashes, normalization/alias grouping, filtering, strata/seeds, CPU dependencies and commands; planned script-to-table/figure map; license uncertainty and evaluation-setting differences. | `final.evidence.episodes` |\\n+| LLM Usage | Disclose documented ideation, code preparation, query planning, and framing assistance; add writing/figure use only if it actually occurs. Do not invent identities, human checks, or training. | `study.selection_kind`; `study.attempts.total`; `final.evidence.episodes` |\\n+\\n+The listed IDs anchor evaluated outcomes; direct method and provenance details must additionally cite their actual local artifacts in the later evidence map, rather than pretending an episode record itself contains the entire source manifest.\\n+\\n+## Reproducibility and reference handoff\\n+\\n+Use HELM **v1.13.0**, Open LLM contents revision `9c09a7cae43334062a82cb164f2ef255013dafa2`, and the distinct results revision `aa81ecc38fdc5708254b833923368970efdf5ef5`. The final manifest records acquisition on 2026-11-17 and extracted-record SHA-256 `d80abb1b13c6962e15f04d9794fc18fcf39e91cf7c79c679e233d3031f934398`. Preserve each source checksum from `task/resources/final/manifest.json`, and distinguish public repository sizes from the evaluated extracted pools. Existing manifest and raw records support normalization, filtering, alias grouping, split, and setting caveats; do not claim perfectly homogeneous evaluation conditions.\\n+\\n+BBH reconciliation matches model revisions but does not prove identical evaluation settings. In the Open LLM auxiliary routing, odd slots use BBH and even slots use the primary-family projection. Do not match auxiliary slots to primary model identities without reconstructing their actual identifiers. Data-specific redistribution permission remains unresolved: public accessibility, code licenses, and model licenses do not establish a score-data redistribution license.\\n+\\n+The writer must create deterministic derived-data/plot/table scripts, record their exact source slices and commands, and provide the dependency versions already available in `task/requirements.txt`. Those manuscript reproduction scripts are not present merely because the evaluated solver exists. Regeneration from existing records is not a new empirical run; any genuinely new analysis must be labeled and grounded separately.\\n+\\n+The bibliography currently provides metadata retrieval, not evidence of substantive reading, and many entries are tangential. Several relevant starter records are absent. Before literature-dependent prose, curate safely and actually read the permitted source; use only available, verified citation keys and do not fabricate positioning or pad related work. This is a writer-stage prerequisite, not a reason to invent a novelty claim now. No external page was accessed during strategy generation. Do not identify or search for the prohibited study, expand citation graphs, or use discussion/aggregation pages; stop and log any accidental exposure.\\n+\\n+## Language guardrails\\n+\\n+**Forbid headings:** Search Progression; Campaign Phases; Milestones; First Valid Result; Timeline; Experiment A; Experiment B; From Baseline to Winner; Optimization Breakthroughs; Successful Certificate Variants.\\n+\\n+**Forbid phrases:** “we then tried,” “first valid result,” “subsequent improvements,” “next-best,” “later variants,” “winning implementation,” “state of the art,” “universally most robust aggregation,” “median always requires more investment,” “measured training cost,” “causal contamination effect,” and “all full-panel solutions are optimal.”\\n+\\n+Private-only terminology exclusions for manuscript prose: `correctness rate`, `correct and eligible`, `eligible`, `combined_score`, `rubric`, `worker_01`, and `worker_02`. Prefer target attainment rate, support fraction, strict first place, exact minimum support, certified infeasibility, and feasible support interval.\\n+\\n+## Completion boundary\\n+\\n+This strategy supports a coherent conditional scientific paper, not a claim of conference acceptance or an already-complete reproduction package. Core limitations, unsuccessful search disclosure, all-target attainment, conditioning definitions, and exact-versus-bounded scope remain in the main paper. No manuscript, claim-mapping JSON, figure, or new research experiment is produced here, and final-paper validation is not run. Bibliographic substantive reading, plotting scripts, manuscript drafting, and later validation remain downstream work.\\n*** End Patch'\\\"'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"Success. Updated the following files:\\nA /workspace/paper/paper_strategy.json\\nA /workspace/paper/paper_strategy.md\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n74:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_48\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/sh -lc \\\"python .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py --global-memory-md /workspace/investigation/memory.md --global-memory-jsonl /workspace/investigation/memory.jsonl --event-json '{\\\\\\\"step\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"final\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"scope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"paper\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"summary\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"paper_strategy_ready: wrote matching standalone strategy memo and JSON centered on exact response-dependent aggregation contrasts. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Planning and record summarization do not establish a new experimental recommendation.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Created paper_strategy.md and paper_strategy.json. Lightweight checks passed JSON structure, all registered source IDs, nonempty supplement, exactly one concept-figure plan, readability budgets, paired selected-support sign checks and nonempty three-rule cohorts. Source diff confirms final/search evaluator scientific logic identical apart from plane/seeds/budgets. Final qualification is independently recorded completed/qualified/true, search selection remains baseline with no winner. Preserved unknown failed-alternative causes, unverified candidate-diagnostic trust, exact versus bounded costs, conditional uncertainty, bibliography reading gaps, data licensing and distinct BBH scope. Main budget 8.5 pages under inspected 5.5-inch single-column ICLR geometry. No manuscript, claim-mapping file, plots, external retrieval, new research experiment or final-paper validation produced. Missing shell apply_patch was resolved using the installed Codex binary apply-patch entrypoint.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"next_action\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Writer should use this strategy contract, safely curate/read relevant permitted references, generate reproducible derived comparisons and figures, and draft the anonymized paper without strengthening claims beyond the recorded exact/interval scopes.\\\\\\\"}'\\n/usr/local/lib/node_modules/@openai/codex/node_modules/@openai/codex-linux-x64/vendor/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/bin/codex --codex-run-as-apply-patch '*** Begin Patch\\n*** Delete File: /tmp/paper_strategy_patch_probe\\n*** End Patch'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n75:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_48\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/sh -lc \\\"python .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py --global-memory-md /workspace/investigation/memory.md --global-memory-jsonl /workspace/investigation/memory.jsonl --event-json '{\\\\\\\"step\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"final\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"scope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"paper\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"summary\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"paper_strategy_ready: wrote matching standalone strategy memo and JSON centered on exact response-dependent aggregation contrasts. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Planning and record summarization do not establish a new experimental recommendation.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Created paper_strategy.md and paper_strategy.json. Lightweight checks passed JSON structure, all registered source IDs, nonempty supplement, exactly one concept-figure plan, readability budgets, paired selected-support sign checks and nonempty three-rule cohorts. Source diff confirms final/search evaluator scientific logic identical apart from plane/seeds/budgets. Final qualification is independently recorded completed/qualified/true, search selection remains baseline with no winner. Preserved unknown failed-alternative causes, unverified candidate-diagnostic trust, exact versus bounded costs, conditional uncertainty, bibliography reading gaps, data licensing and distinct BBH scope. Main budget 8.5 pages under inspected 5.5-inch single-column ICLR geometry. No manuscript, claim-mapping file, plots, external retrieval, new research experiment or final-paper validation produced. Missing shell apply_patch was resolved using the installed Codex binary apply-patch entrypoint.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"next_action\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Writer should use this strategy contract, safely curate/read relevant permitted references, generate reproducible derived comparisons and figures, and draft the anonymized paper without strengthening claims beyond the recorded exact/interval scopes.\\\\\\\"}'\\n/usr/local/lib/node_modules/@openai/codex/node_modules/@openai/codex-linux-x64/vendor/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/bin/codex --codex-run-as-apply-patch '*** Begin Patch\\n*** Delete File: /tmp/paper_strategy_patch_probe\\n*** End Patch'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"Success. Updated the following files:\\nD /tmp/paper_strategy_patch_probe\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
