tion.correct', 'final.qualification.outcome', 'final.qualification.status', 'result.best_any_score', 'result.total_attempts', 'result.total_correct_programs', 'result.total_evaluated_programs', 'result.total_ideas', 'study.attempts.scored', 'study.attempts.total', 'study.attempts.unscored', 'study.baseline_score', 'study.final.correct', 'study.final.outcome', 'study.final.status', 'study.investigation_outcome', 'study.search_score', 'study.search_score_delta', 'study.selection_kind']\nconcept {'figure_id': 'investment_overview', 'required': True, 'purpose': 'Make the counterfactual investment object, fixed-rival assumption, aggregation conditions, and certificate outcomes legible before quantitative results.', 'figure_type': 'diagram', 'preferred_generator': 'generate-concept-figure', 'group_by': 'score intervention and certificate scope', 'metric': 'none; qualitative specification only', 'split_by': 'fixed scores, bounded intervention, aggregation and support outcome', 'preferred_span': 'full_width', 'target_width_fraction': 1.0, 'layout_rationale': 'In the inspected single-column ICLR style, full width is 5.5 inches, not a two-column spread. Use a shallow approximately 5.5-by-1.8-inch diagram on page 1 or 2; a half-width 2.75-inch rendering would compress the update equation and outcome labels. Keep at most six visual groups and three aggregator branches, with at least 9-point rendered labels.', 'allow_progression': False, 'max_panels': 1, 'max_panels_per_row': 1, 'max_categories_per_panel': 6, 'max_series_per_panel': 3, 'source_ids': ['final.evidence.episodes'], 'content_constraints': 'Show x_j changing to x_j+alpha(1-x_j) only on the selected support and label rivals fixed. Three aggregators are conditions, not sequential improvements. Distinguish exact, infeasible, and bounded outcomes. Do not draw training, an architecture transition, a novel certificate mechanism, or numerical toy measurements.'}\nmanifest keys\ndict_keys(['schema_version', 'data_sha256', 'acquired_utc', 'normalization', 'split', 'own_content_hashes', 'disjoint_content_verified', 'sources', 'license_assessment', 'reconciliation', 'sensitivity_limit', 'conference', 'limitations', 'protocol_policy', 'other_content_hashes_commitment_sha256', 'split_attestation'])\n{'schema_version': 1, 'data_sha256': 'd80abb1b13c6962e15f04d9794fc18fcf39e91cf7c79c679e233d3031f934398', 'acquired_utc': '2026-11-17T11:35:39.193972+00:00', 'split': 'Connected components under model alias, raw normalized component and score-map content identities; deterministic sha256 split-v1-38271, modulo3=0 search, otherwise final. All repeated revisions and selected results grouped with their contents row.', 'disjoint_content_verified': True, 'license_assessment': 'Public unauthenticated leaderboard score facts are used for noncommercial reproducible research with attribution. No separate score-data license identified; code/model licenses do not transfer. Derived raw-row extracts, not full mirrors; redistribution permission remains uncertain and must be reviewed before public release.', 'reconciliation': {'revision_matched': 87, 'revision_mismatch_excluded': 3}, 'sensitivity_limit': 'Selected 90 deterministic lexicographically spaced models, latest available result per model at pinned results commit. Keep only exact model-sha matches and complete 24-BBH panels. Contents and results are distinct runs; no claim of equal evaluation settings or score equality. Sensitivity is separately reported, not scored or merged into primary six-task scores.', 'conference': {'url': 'https://media.neurips.cc/Conferences/NeurIPS2026/Formatting_Instructions_For_NeurIPS_2026.zip', 'sha256': '82473931e3ef710fcd3f4a8cd4119b9de32e56825f90f9e5a6d55f2d01b817d9', 'body_pages': 9, 'checklist_required': True}, 'limitations': ['No actual training; coordinate-support uplift is a conditional model, not contamination causality or monetary investment.', 'No scientific performance minimum is delegated; eligibility checks integrity/validity only.', 'Trusted median/trimmed lower bounds may be conservative; exact six-coordinate audits do not prove full-panel optimality.', 'No forbidden literature was searched or accessed; named score assets and official conference formatting only.', 'HELM observed mean in-context counts vary slightly on a few runs; raw denominators, training counts and run specs are retained. Public snapshot scores are not assumed to come from perfectly homogeneous model evaluation conditions.'], 'protocol_policy': {'episodes': 'Case order HELM then OpenLLM, ordinary/constant/copy/permutation, seeds in declared order, then sole first-episode reset replay. Every reset, including the terminal replay, belongs to the complete global contract reset sequence across proxies, connections and process restarts. Replay has statistical weight zero and remains a required validity gate.', 'rpc_operation_table_per_episode': {'reset': 1, 'upload_including_start': 64, 'run_including_commit': 1, 'read': 16, 'release': 1}, 'search_total_calls': 1411, 'final_total_calls': 2075, 'smoke_total_calls': 747, 'max_input_chunks': 64, 'max_output_chunks': 16, 'chunk_decoded_bytes': 1048576, 'output_logical_limit': 16777216, 'input_logical_limit': 67108864, 'controls': ['constant ceiling: no strict winner', 'copy alpha=0: nonleader cannot improve', 'joint nonidentity value-changing column permutation: matched exact-projection feasibility, verified bound and returned cost invariant', 'reset replay: same logical plans/status/bounds from first seed'], 'validity': 'Honest bounded intervals are allowed, including on small audits; never require a comparative search margin. Independently verified claims and matched control consistency gate correctness, not minimum effort performance.', 'aggregation': 'Equal alpha, rule, target, statistical seed; cases 0.7/0.1/0.1/0.1; families 0.5/0.5. Auxiliary decisions unscored validity/sensitivity. Replay weight zero. Failed episode retains utility/feasibility/control=0 and effort/gap=1.', 'uncertainty': '200 paired cluster-bootstrap resamples, RNG48271, per-family/seed/rule/alpha candidate-minus-baseline effort, percentile95. Conditional on fixed rival pools and snapshots; not population/dataset-independent confidence or a significance gate.', 'minimum_productive_baseline_seconds': None, 'calibration': 'No productive-time minimum or comparative threshold delegated by task.md; no artificial floor imposed. Productive baseline loops separately measured, excluding imports/reset/startup/cleanup/output.', 'matched_method_reservations': 'All four methods receive 5 seconds per 12 targets (216 primary-plus-auxiliary decisions), hence search 5 seconds and final 10 seconds; smoke 1 second. Existing wall/CPU ceilings, reference/scoring allowances, cleanup and reset reserves are unchanged. Joint conservative requirements: search 485.9/900 seconds, final 1199.5/1800 seconds, smoke 110.3/120 seconds. Candidate run.work_seconds supplies the positive finite remaining method seconds after uploads; all transport, solve, reads and release share this reservation. It carries no plane or seed mapping.'}, 'other_content_hashes_commitment_sha256': 'ed6fd99c3503515be6e81717d6b76c74d7758fe2072a356931bcc8e8b6a22a7d', 'split_attestation': 'Draft-time paired raw-content audit found zero shared normalized hashes across the frozen roots, also grouping aliases and component ancestry. Counterpart membership/content is sealed; only its SHA256 commitment is present here. Wrapper binds this attestation and own raw rows by artifact hashes.'}\nrecords structure <class 'dict'>\nreference record {'citation_count': 637, 'citation_key': 'López-Pintado2009OnTC', 'id': 'ref.s2.ae67b341dbffd04d883b831bf77179cf710bbeec', 'paper_id': 'ae67b341dbffd04d883b831bf77179cf710bbeec', 'query': 'median trimmed mean finite-sample replacement breakdown order statistics', 'retrieved_at': '2026-11-17T13:24:19.077271+00:00', 'source_url': 'https://api.semanticscholar.org/graph/v1/paper/ae67b341dbffd04d883b831bf77179cf710bbeec?fields=paperId%2Ctitle%2Cyear%2Cvenue%2CcitationCount%2CcitationStyles%2Curl', 'title': 'On the Concept of Depth for Functional Data', 'venue': '', 'year': 2009}\n        raise\n    except (RuntimeError, TimeoutError) as error:\n        category = \"baseline_timeout\" if isinstance(error, TimeoutError) else \"baseline_result_failure\"\n        fail_required_baseline(category, cancel_work, record_failure)\n\n\ndef guard_required_baseline(call, failure_category, cancel_work, record_failure):\n    def check():\n        category = failure_category()\n        if category is not None:\n            fail_required_baseline(category, cancel_work, record_failure)\n    def guarded(request):\n        check()\n        result = call(request)\n        check()\n        return result\n    return guarded\n\n\nclass BrokerTransportFailure(RuntimeError):\n    def __init__(self, operation):\n        self.operation = bounded_failure_name(operation, \"unknown\")\n        super().__init__(\"broker_transport\")\n\n\nclass ProtocolFailure(RuntimeError):\n    def __init__(self, category=\"malformed_response\"):\n        self.category = bounded_failure_name(category, \"malformed_response\")\n        super().__init__(self.category)\n\n\nclass BoundedWorkerStderr:\n    LIMIT = 4096\n\n    def __init__(self, stream):\n        self.stream = stream\n        self.fd = stream.fileno()\n        os.set_blocking(self.fd, False)\n        self.lines = collections.deque()\n        self.pending = bytearray()\n        self.dropping_line = False\n        self.observed_bytes = 0\n        self.retained_bytes = 0\n        self.truncated = False\n        self.capture_error = None\n        self.stop = threading.Event()\n        self.result = None\n        self.reader = threading.Thread(target=self._drain, name=\"worker-stderr-reader\")\n        self.reader.start()\n\n    def _accept(self, chunk):\n        self.observed_bytes += len(chunk)\n        for segment in chunk.splitlines(keepends=True):\n            complete = segment.endswith(b\"\\n\")\n            if not self.dropping_line:\n                if len(self.pending) + len(segment) > self.LIMIT:\n                    self.pending.clear()\n                    self.dropping_line = True\n                    self.truncated = True\n                else:\n                    self.pending.extend(segment)\n            if complete:\n                if not self.dropping_line:\n                    line = bytes(self.pending).decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n                    size = len(line.encode(\"utf-8\"))\n                    if size <= self.LIMIT:\n                        while self.retained_bytes + size > self.LIMIT:\n                            self.retained_bytes -= len(self.lines.popleft().encode(\"utf-8\"))\n                            self.truncated = True\n                        self.lines.append(line)\n                        self.retained_bytes += size\n                    else:\n                        self.truncated = True\n                self.pending.clear()\n                self.dropping_line = False\n\n    def _drain(self):\n        try:\n            with selectors.DefaultSelector() as selector:\n                selector.register(self.fd, selectors.EVENT_READ)\n                while not self.stop.is_set():\n                    if not selector.select(timeout=.05):\n                        continue\n                    try:\n                        chunk = os.read(self.fd, 8192)\n                    except BlockingIOError:\n                        continue\n                    if not chunk:\n                        return\n                    self._accept(chunk)\n                self.capture_error = \"reader_stopped_before_eof\"\n                self.truncated = True\n        except (OSError, ValueError):\n            self.capture_error = \"stderr_capture_failed\"\n            self.truncated = True\n        finally:\n            if self.pending or self.dropping_line:\n                self.truncated = True\n            self.pending.clear()\n            self.stream.close()\n\n    def close(self):\n        if self.result is not None:\n            return dict(self.result)\n        self.reader.join(timeout=.2)\n        if self.reader.is_alive():\n            self.stop.set()\n            self.reader.join(timeout=.2)\n        if self.reader.is_alive():\n            raise RuntimeError(\"stderr reader cleanup unresolved\")\n        self.result = {\"stderr\": \"\".join(self.lines), \"observed_bytes\": self.observed_bytes,\n                       \"retained_bytes\": self.retained_bytes, \"truncated\": self.truncated,\n                       \"capture_error\": self.capture_error}\n        return dict(self.result)\n\n\ndef report_worker_exception(error):\n    name = type(error).__name__\n    if not name.isascii() or not name.isidentifier() or len(name) > 80:\n        name = \"WorkerException\"\n    try:\n        message = str(error)\n    except Exception:\n        message = \"<exception message unavailable>\"\n    if len(message) > 2048 or len(message.encode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")) > 2048:\n        message = \"<exception message omitted: too large>\"\n    print(f\"worker_exception type={name}\\n{message}\", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)\n\n\ndef bounded_json_line(value, wire_limit=WIRE_LIMIT):\n    encoded = json.dumps(value, allow_nan=False, separators=(\",\", \":\")).encode(\"utf-8\") + b\"\\n\"\n    if len(encoded) >= wire_limit:\n        raise ProtocolFailure(\"wire_limit\")\n    return encoded\n\n\n# scientific-evidence\n\nThis is the canonical generated spec bundle for the `scientific-evidence` skill.\nUse the skill script as the source of truth for schemas, layout, and wording.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis contract is generic and file-format-agnostic.\nIt supports inline evidence refs in text-like files, adjacent `.prov.json` sidecars for generated artifacts, and a central JSONL ledger.\n\n## Why this exists\n\nThe point of `scientific-evidence` is to make an agent leave a machine-checkable trail for important numbers, figures, tables, and derived outputs.\nA paper or report should not depend on free-form prose alone when those claims can point back to real artifacts.\nAlways use this contract during paper writing whenever the agent adds manuscript numbers, table values, figure inputs, or derived statistics.\n\n## Fixed directory structure\n\n```text\nscientific-evidence/\n  spec.md\n  bundle.manifest.json\n  ledger.jsonl\n  schemas/\n    evidence-reference.schema.json\n    artifact-manifest.schema.json\n    ledger-entry.schema.json\n    verification-report.schema.json\n```\n\nAgents should use this layout exactly. Do not invent alternate bundle directories.\n\n## Grammar\n\n```text\nEvidenceRef   := '@evidence[[' Target [ '#' Locator ] ']]'\nTarget        := non-empty path | absolute path | URI | stable identifier\nLocator       := opaque fragment without closing ']]'\nSidecar       := '<artifact>.prov.json'\nLedger        := 'scientific-evidence/ledger.jsonl'\n```\n\n### Notes\n\n- `Target` stays generic. The verifier may classify it as `path`, `absolute-path`, `uri`, `id`, or `unknown`.\n- `Locator` is opaque unless a verifier adapter knows how to interpret it.\n- Text-like artifacts should use inline `@evidence[[...]]` refs. Binary or generated outputs should carry an adjacent `.prov.json` sidecar.\n\n### Minimal examples\n\n- `@evidence[[TARGET]]`\n- `@evidence[[TARGET#LOCATOR]]`\n- `figure.png.prov.json`\n\n## Verification behavior\n\nA verifier uses this bundle to inspect whether the agent left a connected evidence trail.\nThe base verifier uses three reference states:\n\n- `resolved`: the target exists and the verifier can validate the locator semantics it understands.\n- `anchored`: the target exists, but only path/hash checks were possible or the locator remained opaque.\n- `dangling`: the target does not resolve, the sidecar chain breaks, or the reference is malformed.\n\n### Minimum verifier expectations\n\n1. Resolve every inline evidence ref to a target path, URI, or id when possible.\n2. Mark each ref as `resolved`, `anchored`, or `dangling`.\n3. For manifests, require every `derived_from` edge to resolve to at least `anchored`.\n4. When hashes are recorded, compare them. Missing hashes are allowed.\n5. Do not pretend to interpret unknown locator grammars. Keep them `anchored` unless an adapter proves more.\n\n### What verification should prove\n\nAt a minimum, a downstream verifier should be able to:\n\n- scan text-like artifacts for `@evidence[[...]]` refs\n- read `.prov.json` sidecars for generated artifacts\n- resolve refs against real files or stable ids\n- classify each link as `resolved`, `anchored`, or `dangling`\n- fail when a generated artifact has no input trail or when a claimed source does not exist\n\nThis does not prove every scientific claim automatically. It proves whether the agent left enough structure for later auditing and stricter replay.\nA core paper-writing policy is: do not hardcode result numbers inside plotting or calculation scripts when those values should come from real artifacts. Read from files and leave matching `@evidence[[...]]` refs near the read or derivation logic.\n\n## Schema set\n\nThe generated bundle includes:\n\n- `schemas/evidence-reference.schema.json`\n- `schemas/artifact-manifest.schema.json`\n- `schemas/ledger-entry.schema.json`\n- `schemas/verification-report.schema.json`\n- `spec.md`\n- `bundle.manifest.json`\n- `ledger.jsonl`\n\n### Schema intent\n\n- `evidence-reference`: parsed form of one inline `@evidence[[...]]` token.\n- `artifact-manifest`: canonical sidecar schema for `<artifact>.prov.json`.\n- `ledger-entry`: one JSONL row in `scientific-evidence/ledger.jsonl`.\n- `verification-report`: verifier output with per-reference results and summary counts.\n\n## Examples across file formats\n\n### Python\n\n```python\n# Read the metric from disk; do not hardcode 96.7 here.\n# @evidence[[results/metrics.json#mnist.accuracy_mean]]\nimport json\npayload = json.loads(open(\"results/metrics.json\", encoding=\"utf-8\").read())\nvalue = payload[\"mnist\"][\"accuracy_mean\"]\n```\n\n### Bash\n\n```bash\n# @evidence[[results/run_summary.csv#row(dataset=mnist,variant=proposed).accuracy]]\npython scripts/summarize_results.py --input results/run_summary.csv\n```\n\n### LaTeX\n\n```tex\nAccuracy reached 96.7\\%. % @evidence[[generated/stats.json#mnist.accuracy_mean]]\n```\n\n### Markdown\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
