{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport requests\nu='https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.03300';r=requests.get(u,timeout=30);print(r.status_code);from bs4 import BeautifulSoup\ns=BeautifulSoup(r.text,'html.parser');print(s.select_one('blockquote.abstract').get_text(' ',strip=True) if s.select_one('blockquote.abstract') else r.text[:100])\nPY\npython .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py --help\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('task/resources/final/manifest.json'))\nfor k in ['normalization','protocol_policy','sources']:\n v=p[k]; print(k,str(v)[:4500])\nr=json.load(open('task/resources/final/records.json'));print('RECORDS',[(k,type(v).__name__,len(v) if hasattr(v,'__len__') else 0) for k,v in r.items()] if isinstance(r,dict) else str(r[0])[:600])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport requests\nu='https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.03300';r=requests.get(u,timeout=30);print(r.status_code);from bs4 import BeautifulSoup\ns=BeautifulSoup(r.text,'html.parser');print(s.select_one('blockquote.abstract').get_text(' ',strip=True) if s.select_one('blockquote.abstract') else r.text[:100])\nPY\npython .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py --help\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('task/resources/final/manifest.json'))\nfor k in ['normalization','protocol_policy','sources']:\n v=p[k]; print(k,str(v)[:4500])\nr=json.load(open('task/resources/final/records.json'));print('RECORDS',[(k,type(v).__name__,len(v) if hasattr(v,'__len__') else 0) for k,v in r.items()] if isinstance(r,dict) else str(r[0])[:600])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"200\nAbstract: We propose a new test to measure a text model's multitask accuracy. The test covers 57 tasks including elementary mathematics, US history, computer science, law, and more. To attain high accuracy on this test, models must possess extensive world knowledge and problem solving ability. We find that while most recent models have near random-chance accuracy, the very largest GPT-3 model improves over random chance by almost 20 percentage points on average. However, on every one of the 57 tasks, the best models still need substantial improvements before they can reach expert-level accuracy. Models also have lopsided performance and frequently do not know when they are wrong. Worse, they still have near-random accuracy on some socially important subjects such as morality and law. By comprehensively evaluating the breadth and depth of a model's academic and professional understanding, our test can be used to analyze models across many tasks and to identify important shortcomings.\nusage: append_memory.py [-h] [--write-conclusions] [--event-json EVENT_JSON]\n                        [--event-file EVENT_FILE]\n                        [--local-memory-md LOCAL_MEMORY_MD]\n                        [--global-memory-md GLOBAL_MEMORY_MD]\n                        [--global-memory-jsonl GLOBAL_MEMORY_JSONL]\n                        [--conclusions-md CONCLUSIONS_MD]\n                        [--conclusions-history-jsonl CONCLUSIONS_HISTORY_JSONL]\n                        [--conclusions-text CONCLUSIONS_TEXT]\n                        [--cycle-index CYCLE_INDEX]\n                        [--worker-index WORKER_INDEX]\n                        [--gate-trigger GATE_TRIGGER]\n                        [--gate-reason GATE_REASON]\n\nAppend one memory event, or atomically rewrite conclusions.md.\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --write-conclusions   Switch into conclusions-write mode (validates and\n                        replaces conclusions.md).\n  --event-json EVENT_JSON\n                        Event payload as JSON object string\n  --event-file EVENT_FILE\n                        Path to event JSON file\n  --local-memory-md LOCAL_MEMORY_MD\n                        Local workspace memory markdown path\n  --global-memory-md GLOBAL_MEMORY_MD\n                        Global markdown memory path (event mode)\n  --global-memory-jsonl GLOBAL_MEMORY_JSONL\n                        Global JSONL memory path (event mode)\n  --conclusions-md CONCLUSIONS_MD\n                        Path of conclusions.md to overwrite (--write-\n                        conclusions mode)\n  --conclusions-history-jsonl CONCLUSIONS_HISTORY_JSONL\n                        Path of conclusions_history.jsonl to append a record\n                        to\n  --conclusions-text CONCLUSIONS_TEXT\n                        Conclusion paragraph (omit to read from stdin)\n  --cycle-index CYCLE_INDEX\n                        Current cycle index for the history record\n  --worker-index WORKER_INDEX\n                        Current worker index for the history record\n  --gate-trigger GATE_TRIGGER\n                        Gate trigger letter (a|b|c|d) recorded in history\n  --gate-reason GATE_REASON\n                        One-sentence reason for the update; for trigger d name\n                        the dimension\nnormalization NFKC, whitespace collapse, LF, recursively sorted canonical JSON, integer-valued floats canonicalized to integers; no tokenization. Component hashes strip identifying cells/metadata; score-map hashes include task values and settings. Full raw source rows retained. Null distinct from missing.\nprotocol_policy {'episodes': 'Case order HELM then OpenLLM, ordinary/constant/copy/permutation, seeds in declared order, then sole first-episode reset replay. Every reset, including the terminal replay, belongs to the complete global contract reset sequence across proxies, connections and process restarts. Replay has statistical weight zero and remains a required validity gate.', 'rpc_operation_table_per_episode': {'reset': 1, 'upload_including_start': 64, 'run_including_commit': 1, 'read': 16, 'release': 1}, 'search_total_calls': 1411, 'final_total_calls': 2075, 'smoke_total_calls': 747, 'max_input_chunks': 64, 'max_output_chunks': 16, 'chunk_decoded_bytes': 1048576, 'output_logical_limit': 16777216, 'input_logical_limit': 67108864, 'controls': ['constant ceiling: no strict winner', 'copy alpha=0: nonleader cannot improve', 'joint nonidentity value-changing column permutation: matched exact-projection feasibility, verified bound and returned cost invariant', 'reset replay: same logical plans/status/bounds from first seed'], 'validity': 'Honest bounded intervals are allowed, including on small audits; never require a comparative search margin. Independently verified claims and matched control consistency gate correctness, not minimum effort performance.', 'aggregation': 'Equal alpha, rule, target, statistical seed; cases 0.7/0.1/0.1/0.1; families 0.5/0.5. Auxiliary decisions unscored validity/sensitivity. Replay weight zero. 