gs.\\\", EPISODES, [\\\"source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L672-L745\\\", \\\"derived/summary.json#seeds\\\"], []),\n+    (\\\"Full-support failure certifies unattainability for these monotone aggregators; it is not merely a limited-search failure.\\\", EPISODES, [\\\"source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py#L99-L108\\\"], []),\n+    (\\\"The selected implementation enumerates supports up to six coordinates, solves larger means exactly by sorted headroom, and uses marginal greedy witnesses for larger order-statistic panels.\\\", EPISODES, [\\\"source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py#L109-L137\\\"], []),\n+    (\\\"Lower bounds are independently verified reference bounds; feasible large-panel order-statistic supports are upper bounds, not exact costs.\\\", EPISODES, [\\\"source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L761-L789\\\", \\\"source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L873-L925\\\"], []),\n+    (\\\"The fixed jointly attainable mean-median cohorts contain 18, 17, and 17 targets, and every cost included in their contrast is exact.\\\", EPISODES, [\\\"derived/summary.json#central\\\"], []),\n+    (\\\"In each fixed six-task cohort the average median-minus-mean support fraction is negative at half headroom and positive at full headroom; all reported values and abstract ranges are derived from the same exact contrasts.\\\", EPISODES, [\\\"derived/summary.json#central\\\", \\\"figures/exact_rule_contrast.pdf\\\"], []),\n+    (\\\"The primary grid contains 72 target decisions per rule-ceiling cell, not necessarily independent unique models.\\\", EPISODES, [\\\"derived/summary.json#grid\\\"], []),\n+    (\\\"Open LLM attainment counts at quarter, half, and full headroom differ across mean, median, and trimming as reported in the main text and complete grid.\\\", EPISODES, [\\\"derived/summary.json#grid\\\", \\\"derived/full_grid.tex\\\"], []),\n+    (\\\"HELM attainment counts at quarter, half, and full headroom are those in the main text and complete grid; all ordinary primary nonattainment is certified infeasible.\\\", EPISODES, [\\\"derived/summary.json#grid\\\", \\\"derived/full_grid.tex\\\"], []),\n+    (\\\"All primary targets attain first place at full headroom in the recorded panels.\\\", EPISODES, [\\\"derived/summary.json#grid\\\"], []),\n+    (\\\"Figure 3 certification intervals use equal seed weights and within-ceiling three-rule joint cohorts; the caption reports all cohort sizes.\\\", EPISODES, [\\\"derived/summary.json#support\\\", \\\"figures/attainability_and_support_scope.pdf\\\"], []),\n+    (\\\"HELM half-headroom order-statistic average upper bounds lie below the exact mean cost on the joint cohort, while full-headroom intervals overlap the mean and do not establish reversal of minimum costs.\\\", EPISODES, [\\\"derived/summary.json#support\\\"], []),\n+    (\\\"The reported six-task three-rule support averages are exact within their declared jointly attainable ceiling-specific cohorts, which differ across ceilings.\\\", EPISODES, [\\\"derived/summary.json#support\\\"], []),\n+    (\\\"The main half-headroom table reports all-target penalized effort for exact/witness, marginal greedy, random, and no-intervention policies; nonattainment contributes one.\\\", EPISODES, [\\\"derived/comparators.tex\\\", \\\"source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L873-L925\\\"], []),\n+    (\\\"The frozen procedure ties greedy on HELM and the six-task mean, and has smaller penalized effort on the six-task median and trimmed mean at half headroom.\\\", EPISODES, [\\\"derived/comparators.tex\\\"], []),\n+    (\\\"Every scalar in the complete primary table is reproduced from the ordinary primary evaluator decisions, with success and penalty semantics kept separate.\\\", EPISODES, [\\\"derived/full_grid.tex\\\"], []),\n+    (\\\"Recorded conditional paired policy intervals use 200 cluster bootstrap resamples, RNG seed 48271, and 95-percent percentile endpoints; these do not test cross-rule ordering.\\\", EPISODES, [\\\"source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L1046-L1068\\\", \\\"derived/paired_intervals.tex\\\"], [\\\"Efron\\\"]),\n+    (\\\"Every row of the supplementary policy interval table reproduces the recorded family, rule, ceiling, seed, comparator, difference, and interval endpoints.\\\", EPISODES, [\\\"derived/paired_intervals.tex\\\"], []),\n+    (\\\"Auxiliary HELM projections, Open LLM even slots, and BBH odd slots have separately reported counts; BBH revision matching does not establish identical evaluation settings.\\\", EPISODES, [\\\"derived/auxiliary.tex\\\", \\\"source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L718-L732\\\", \\\"source_evidence/data/manifest.json#reconciliation\\\"], []),\n+    (\\\"The completed final evaluation is qualified; this does not imply unrestricted validity or exact large-panel order-statistic costs.\\\", [\\\"final.qualification.status\\\", \\\"final.qualification.outcome\\\", \\\"final.qualification.correct\\\"], [\\\"paper_data.json#/final_evaluation\\\"], []),\n+    (\\\"The recorded final control pass fraction is one; candidate diagnostics remain unverified.\\\", [\\\"final.metric.control_pass_rate\\\"] + EPISODES, [\\\"paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/metrics/control_pass_rate\\\", \\\"paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/candidate_diagnostics_trust\\\"], []),\n+    (\\\"The retained selection is the reference baseline, with no qualifying development winner and zero retained development-score change.\\\", [\\\"study.selection_kind\\\", \\\"study.investigation_outcome\\\", \\\"study.search_score_delta\\\"], [\\\"paper_data.json#/downstream_study\\\"], []),\n+    (\\\"Three development alternatives were scored and none unscored; their qualification-failure causes are not identified, and they are not controlled component ablations.\\\", [\\\"study.attempts.total\\\", \\\"study.attempts.scored\\\", \\\"study.attempts.unscored\\\", \\\"study.investigation_outcome\\\"], [\\\"paper_data.json#/downstream_study\\\"], []),\n+    (\\\"The reported source locations support the exact evaluated implementation, whose selected and baseline source copies match.\\\", [\\\"study.selection_kind\\\"] + EPISODES, [\\\"source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py\\\", \\\"source_evidence/downstream/baseline/src/program.py\\\"], []),\n+    (\\\"The final evaluator uses CPU computation, its documented wall and method reservations and advisory decision budget; dependency versions are the supplied versions.\\\", EPISODES, [\\\"source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L39-L54\\\", \\\"source_evidence/evaluation/requirements.txt\\\", \\\"derived/environment.json\\\"], []),\n+    (\\\"Raw-score documentation, normalization, content partitioning, and uncertain score-data redistribution rights are as recorded by the acquisition manifest.\\\", EPISODES, [\\\"source_evidence/data/manifest.json\\\"], []),\n+    (\\\"The study does not measure training responses, practical expenditure, causal contamination effects, or population superiority; the observed ordering is conditional and descriptively selected.\\\", EPISODES, [\\\"derived/summary.json#central\\\", \\\"source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py#L16-L28\\\"], []),\n+]\n+\n+\n+def main():\n+    claims = [{\\\"claim\\\": claim, \\\"source_ids\\\": sources, \\\"citation_keys\\\": citations,\n+               \\\"evidence_refs\\\": [\\\"@evidence[[\\\"+path+\\\"]]\\\" for path in paths]}\n+              for claim, sources, paths, citations in CLAIMS]\n+    references = json.loads(Path(\\\"references_provenance.json\\\").read_text())[\\\"references\\\"]\n+    for reference in references:\n+        key = reference[\\\"citation_key\\\"]\n+        claims.append({\\\"claim\\\": \\\"Literature positioning uses only the inspected abstract and canonical metadata of \\\" + reference[\\\"title\\\"] + \\\".\\\",\n+                       \\\"source_ids\\\": [reference[\\\"id\\\"]], \\\"citation_keys\\\": [key],\n+                       \\\"evidence_refs\\\": [\\\"@evidence[[literature/\\\"+key+\\\".json#abstract]]\\\"]})\n+    Path(\\\"claims_grounding.json\\\").write_text(json.dumps({\\\"claims\\\": claims}, indent=2)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\n+\n+\n+if __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\n+    main()\n*** Add File: scripts/fetch_public_inputs.py\n+import argparse\n+import hashlib\n+import json\n+from pathlib import Path\n+from urllib.request import urlopen\n+\n+\n+def main():\n+    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n+    parser.add_argument(\\\"--output\\\", type=Path, required=True)\n+    args = parser.parse_args()\n+    args.output.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n+    # @evidence[[source_evidence/data/manifest.json#sources]]\n+    sources = json.loads(Path(\\\"source_evidence/data/manifest.json\\\").read_text())[\\\"sources\\\"]\n+    for index, source in enumerate(sources):\n+        path = args.output / (str(index).zfill(3) + \\\"_\\\" + source[\\\"sha256\\\"])\n+        if path.exists():\n+            encoded = path.read_bytes()\n+        else:\n+            with urlopen(source[\\\"source\\\"], timeout=120) as response:\n+                encoded = response.read()\n+        actual = hashlib.sha256(encoded).hexdigest()\n+        if actual \"'!= source[\"sha256\"]:\n+            raise RuntimeError(\"Source checksum mismatch: \" + source[\"source\"])\n+        if not path.exists():\n+            path.write_bytes(encoded)\n+        print(index, source[\"family\"], actual)\n+\n+\n+if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n+    main()\n*** Add File: REPRODUCIBILITY.md\n+# Reproducing the manuscript\n+\n+## Scope and entrypoints\n+\n+The empirical evaluation was completed before manuscript writing. This paper step only reaggregates existing recorded observations. It does not rerun scientific evaluations, train models, or manufacture simulated measurements. `paper_data.json` is the immutable evidence registry. `source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py` is the evaluated solver; the adjacent `program_spec.toml` declares its entrypoint. The identical baseline source remains inspectable under `source_evidence/downstream/baseline/`.\n+\n+All manuscript values are produced by `scripts/build_paper_artifacts.py`; claim mappings are produced by `scripts/map_claims.py`. Run from this directory:\n+\n+```sh\n+python3 -m venv /tmp/leaderboard-paper-env\n+/tmp/leaderboard-paper-env/bin/pip install --index-url https://pypi.org/simple -r source_evidence/evaluation/requirements.txt Pillow requests beautifulsoup4 jsonschema\n+/tmp/leaderboard-paper-env/bin/python scripts/build_paper_artifacts.py\n+/tmp/leaderboard-paper-env/bin/python scripts/map_claims.py\n+```\n+\n+The pinned scientific dependencies are NumPy 2.2.6, SciPy 1.15.3, PyArrow 19.0.1, and Matplotlib 3.10.3. The actual paper-analysis Python and additional package versions are in `derived/environment.json`. Install auxiliary dependencies only in a private directory outside the manuscript workspace. Figure/table regeneration is CPU-only and small compared with the original evaluation; its exact runtime depends on the environment. No unmeasured runtime is reported as an empirical result.\n+\n+## Artifact map\n+\n+| Manuscript artifact | Generated output | Inputs / operation |\n+|---|---|---|\n+| Overview figure | `figures/investment_overview.png` | Synchronous orchestrator-owned conceptual illustration; no numerical evidence. The initial image and `{}` prompt log are explicit placeholders. |\n+| Exact contrast figure | `figures/exact_rule_contrast.pdf` and `.png` | Ordinary primary Open LLM decisions; join by seed and slot; require attainability for mean and median at both half and full headroom; verify exact status; average paired support differences. |\n+| Attainment and scope figure | `figures/attainability_and_support_scope.pdf` and `.png` | All ordinary primary decisions for attainment; per-ceiling three-rule joint cohorts for lower/upper support bounds; average seed means equally. |\n+| Main comparator table | `derived/comparators.tex` | Half-headroom primary all-target penalized effort; same target decisions for all policies. |\n+| Complete primary table | `derived/full_grid.tex` | All rule/ceiling primary cells. |\n+| Conditional interval table | `derived/paired_intervals.tex` | Recorded paired policy intervals only; no new bootstrap. |\n+| Auxiliary table | `derived/auxiliary.tex` | HELM auxiliary projection, Open LLM even slots, and BBH odd slots kept separate. |\n+\n+Every numerical row above is generated by `scripts/build_paper_artifacts.py`. It writes linked provenance sidecars, embeds the generated table rows in `paper.tex`, and produces `derived/summary.json`. Re-running it preserves the concept image when the orchestrator completion marker exists; it never writes that marker. Quantitative PDFs are used by LaTeX; PNG exports are 300 DPI. Analysis uses recorded seeds 1009, 1013, and 1019; the recorded policy intervals used seed 48271 and 200 cluster resamples. No new random draws are required for manuscript regeneration.\n+\n+## Public data versions and acquisition\n+\n+`source_evidence/data/manifest.json` preserves all original source URLs, individual SHA-256 checksums, normalization, partitioning, settings, and license assessment. `source_evidence/data/records.json` is the exact frozen extracted input; its SHA-256 is checked by the build script. These are physical evidence copies, not symlinks to external workspace files. The source evaluator and dependency specification are copied without changing their scientific logic into `source_evidence/evaluation/`.\n+\n+- HELM MMLU: `https://storage.googleapis.com/crfm-helm-public/mmlu/benchmark_output/releases/v1.13.0/`; the manifest enumerates subject tables rather than mirroring all run logs.\n+- Open LLM contents: `https://huggingface.co/datasets/open-llm-leaderboard/contents`, revision `9c09a7cae43334062a82cb164f2ef255013dafa2`.\n+- Distinct Open LLM results snapshot: `https://huggingface.co/datasets/open-llm-leaderboard/results`, revision `aa81ecc38fdc5708254b833923368970efdf5ef5`.\n+- Acquisition: `2026-11-17T11:35:39.193972+00:00`. Extracted-record SHA-256: `d80abb1b13c6962e15f04d9794fc18fcf39e91cf7c79c679e233d3031f934398`.\n+\n+@evidence[[source_evidence/data/manifest.json]]\n+\n+To independently retrieve the exact raw source objects and check their recorded checksums, without account access or an entire repository mirror:\n+\n+```sh\n+python scripts/fetch_public_inputs.py --output /tmp/leaderboard-public-source-cache\n+```\n+\n+This acquisition command is supplied for reproduction and was not rerun during paper writing. It fails on changed or unavailable objects instead of silently replacing a snapshot. Exact reconstruction of the evaluated partition is anchored by the supplied raw-row extract and the manifest'\"'s content attestations, not by whatever current leaderboard rows happen to be available. The extracted final pools contain 60 HELM rows, 3057 Open LLM rows, and 53 complete revision-matched BBH rows; the latter is a subset of the Open LLM records. These are extracted pools, not public-repository sizes. Raw contents rows retain unit-interval score values; no cross-task z-score normalization is introduced here.\n+\n+@evidence[[derived/summary.json#pool_counts]]\n+\n+The evaluator's \"'`load_resources`, `select_targets`, and `prepare_episode` functions specify extraction, target strata, semantic columns, and auxiliary routing. In particular, complete BBH panels are in distinct result records, not invented subdivisions of the BBH aggregate. Exact model SHA matching does not imply identical prompt or other settings. Unicode/canonical-JSON normalization, alias/content grouping, and deterministic connected-component partitioning are specified in the manifest. Original acquisition code was not supplied; the frozen raw rows and checksum-verifying download code are provided rather than pretending that a missing acquisition implementation was executed during writing.\n+\n+## Original evaluation reproduction\n+\n+`source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py` is the exact evaluator source, not a manuscript-written approximation. It exposes `--program_path` and `--results_dir`, resolves `TASK_SOURCE_DIR/resources/final`, and requires Linux x86_64 process-isolation facilities and its documented RPC environment. A future full reevaluation can be invoked in a compatible environment with the original task bundle:\n+\n+```sh\n+TASK_SOURCE_DIR=/workspace/task python source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py '\"\\\\\n+  --program_path source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py \\\\\n+  --results_dir /tmp/leaderboard-reevaluation\n+\"'```\n+\n+This is a new evaluation command, **not executed during manuscript preparation**, and is not required for replaying manuscript summaries. The final wall allowance is 1800 seconds, with per-episode matched method reservations and advisory per-decision node budgets specified in source. Results and timing can vary with CPU/process-isolation support. Do not confuse a failure to recreate the isolation environment with measured scientific nonattainment.\n+\n+## References, prohibited-source boundary, and template\n+\n+The initially staged bibliography contained many irrelevant metadata-only matches. It was replaced with 25 targeted, inspected canonical records; `literature/*.json` stores the abstracts actually consulted and complete metadata. Reading was limited to those abstracts and metadata, so no detailed literature theorem or uninspected full-text result is claimed. `scripts/curate_references.py` regenerates the bibliography from the cached records without new network access; on an empty cache it visits only exact canonical identifiers. No citation graph or broad strategic-leaderboard search was used. No prohibited-study exposure was identified. The unsuccessful publisher-abstract access for Huber was resolved through the exact DOI record in OpenAlex; no related works were followed.\n+\n+The manuscript uses the official ICLR 2026 template from the ICLR Master-Template repository, not the NeurIPS template mentioned in the historical data-acquisition manifest. `template_provenance.json` records the exact archive and style-file hashes. ICLR 2026 does not supply a mandatory NeurIPS-style checklist in that template. The manuscript is anonymized and contains an explicit LLM Usage disclosure.\n+\n+## Validation\n+\n+```sh\n+python .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_tex_refs.py --tex paper.tex --bib references.bib\n+python .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py '\"\\\\\n+  --paper-data paper_data.json --references references_provenance.json \\\\\n+  --bib references.bib --claims claims_grounding.json --paper-dir .\n+bash .codex/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.sh verify --root-dir .\n+bash .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/compile_latex.sh paper.tex\n+\"'```\n+\n+Compilation requires a LaTeX distribution, BibTeX, and Poppler `pdftotext`. The supplied canonical compile validator may reject a system TeX configuration symlink that crosses between two otherwise approved TeX installation roots in this container. This is an environment issue, not an unresolved manuscript input. The paper is also compiled with `pdflatex -recorder -no-shell-escape`, BibTeX, and two further LaTeX passes; actual recorder inputs are audited separately. Rendered references, supplement ordering, and body occupancy are checked on the PDF. The concept placeholder is intentionally replaced by the orchestrator before its final compile; it is not a completed scientific figure.\n+\n+## Redistribution and scope limits\n+\n+No separate score-data redistribution license was identified. Public unauthenticated access, repository-code licenses, and model licenses do not settle permissions for these data extracts. Review permission before public redistribution. All conclusions concern frozen score-space counterfactuals, not training expenses, causal contamination, independent training replications, or universal aggregator rankings. Unsuccessful development alternatives have unknown qualification-failure causes; their retained proxy scores are not mixed with sealed final evidence.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\n)\"\n/tmp/paper-venv/bin/python scripts/map_claims.py\npython .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py --paper-data paper_data.json --references references_provenance.json --bib references.bib --claims claims_grounding.json --paper-dir .'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
